var __index = {"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"index.html","title":"Welcome","text":""},{"location":"index.html#acttrader-trader-user-manual","title":"ActTrader Trader User Manual","text":"<p>This manual explains how to use the ActTrader trading platform. Each page covers one task.</p> <ul> <li>Find a topic with the contents on the left, or type in Search at the top. Search looks at every page.</li> <li>Pick dark or light with the sun/moon button at the top. The screenshots switch with it, so they match how your app looks.</li> <li>Watch it being done. Most pages have a short video under the screenshot. Click \u25b6 Watch how to play it on the page.</li> </ul> <p> </p> <p>The Trading tab: the watchlist on the left, the chart, and your positions at the bottom.</p>"},{"location":"index.html#where-to-start","title":"Where to start","text":"If you want to\u2026 Read Log in for the first time Log In Get started in five minutes Quick Start Buy or sell at the current price Open a New Position (Market Order) Be told when a price reaches a level Price Alerts"},{"location":"whats-new.html","title":"What's New","text":""},{"location":"whats-new.html#whats-new","title":"What's New","text":"<p>If you used the previous ActTrader Windows client, the trading itself is unchanged. Dealing Rates is now called the Watchlist, and Balance, Equity, Usable Margin, Used Margin, Net P/L and Rollover Time mean exactly what they did before. What has changed is how the application is arranged.</p>"},{"location":"whats-new.html#one-window-eight-tabs","title":"One window, eight tabs","text":"<p>The old client opened each function in its own floating window. ActTrader now has eight fixed tabs across the top: Trading, Instruments, Summary, Reports, ActFX, Living Market, Analytics and Marketplace. Everything is one click away, and nothing gets lost behind another window.</p> <p>You can still use separate windows: most panels can be moved out to a second monitor and put back when you are done. See Floating Windows.</p>"},{"location":"whats-new.html#new-features","title":"New features","text":"Feature What it gives you Living Market A live map of currency strength: which currencies are driving the market and how pairs relate. Analytics Your trading performance at a glance: win rate, profit factor, equity curve, a trading calendar and an AI health score. Strategy Marketplace Ready-made strategies to add with one click, free trials of paid ones, and a place to share or sell your own. Your strategies follow you to any computer. ActAI Describe a trading strategy in plain English. ActAI shows its plan, then writes the strategy and checks that it works. Voice commands Speak an instruction instead of clicking. Every trading action is shown for you to confirm first. Command palette Press Ctrl+K and type an instruction, such as buy 0.01 eurusd or chart gbpusd. Price alerts on the server Your alerts are kept by your broker, so they are still there the next time you log in. Quick Trade Trade with a single click on a price, without the order ticket. Multiple accounts Switch between your accounts from the top-left menu. Each keeps its own layout and watchlists. Pivot points Five pivot formulas on the Instruments tab's detail panel. Bar Replay Replay the market candle by candle on the chart, to practise or check an idea. Indicator templates Save a set of indicators and put it on any chart. More than a hundred indicators. Chart Settings Colours with a palette, status line, Bid/Ask lines, grid and watermark, settings templates, apply to all charts. Go to a date Jump the chart to any day; older history loads automatically. Guided tours The ? button at the right of the tab row walks you through the tab you are on. Update check The Help panel tells you when a new version is available, with a Download button."},{"location":"whats-new.html#where-familiar-features-are-now","title":"Where familiar features are now","text":"In the previous client Now Dealing Rates The Watchlist on the Trading tab Open Positions, Orders, Closed Positions The Open, Pending and Closed tabs at the bottom of the Trading tab (details) Summary, Events and Messages, Risk Exposure The Summary tab, all on one screen Instruments The Instruments tab, with a detail panel Reports The Reports tab Price Alerts Set from any instrument; listed on the Summary tab (Price Alerts) ActFX and the MQL4 converter The ActFX tab Profiles The Profiles icon on the right-hand strip (Layout and Profiles) Default stop / limit distances Settings \u2192 Trading \u2192 Default Orders Distance (details) Default Trader Range Settings \u2192 Trading (Settings)"},{"location":"actfx/index.html","title":"ActFX Automated Strategies","text":""},{"location":"actfx/index.html#actfx-automated-strategies","title":"ActFX Automated Strategies","text":"<p>ActFX lets you run trading strategies written in a scripting language. The tab has four sub-tabs:</p> <p>Strategies  \u00b7  Editor  \u00b7  Tester  \u00b7  ActAI</p> <p>The Strategies sub-tab shows a count of the strategies you have running.</p> <p> </p> <p>Your strategies on the left: Purchased first, then My Strategies. The selected strategy's Run, Edit, Test and Improve buttons are on the right.</p> Watch how: ActFX overview (0:42) <p></p> <p>ActFX lists your own strategies and the ones you bought. Ready-made strategies, including the fourteen supplied by ActTrader, are in the Strategy Marketplace. Add one there and it appears here.</p> <p>The toolbar above the sub-tabs has:</p> Button What it does \u21c4 MQL\u2192ActFX Opens the MetaTrader converter (see Converting MetaTrader Strategies). Shortcut Ctrl+Shift+M. + New Creates a strategy, blank or from a template. Shortcut Ctrl+N. \u21e5 Import Adds a strategy file (.acts or .actlib) to your library. \u229e Compile Checks the strategy for errors. Shown only on the Editor sub-tab. Shortcut F9. \u229e+ Add Compiles the strategy and adds it to My Strategies. Shown only on the Editor sub-tab. Search box \"Search strategies\u2026\" \u2014 finds a strategy by name. Shown only on the Strategies sub-tab. \u21bb Refresh Reloads the list and saves your strategies to your account, so they appear when you log in on another computer."},{"location":"actfx/index.html#strategy-times","title":"Strategy times","text":"<p>A strategy reads hours and dates in the time zone set in Settings \u2192 Account: My Computer, Server Time or Custom. If you change it, running strategies use the new zone straight away.</p>"},{"location":"actfx/index.html#in-this-section","title":"In this section","text":"Page The Strategy Library Your strategies, new ones, copies Running and Stopping Strategies Run a strategy, watch it, stop it safely Editor and Tester Write a strategy and test it on past prices ActAI Describe a strategy in plain English and let ActAI write it Converting MetaTrader Strategies Turn an MT4/MT5 expert into an ActFX strategy"},{"location":"actfx/actai.html","title":"ActAI","text":""},{"location":"actfx/actai.html#actai","title":"ActAI","text":"<p>ActAI writes strategy code from a plain-English description. Type what you want \u2014 or click one of the example ideas \u2014 and press Send (or Enter). For a new strategy ActAI first replies with a short plan listing the rules and settings it understood. Click \"\u2713 Generate strategy\" if it is right, or \"Change parameters\u2026\" to correct it. The generated code is compiled automatically and, if it fails, ActAI is asked to fix it. Buttons let you copy the code or open it in the Editor.</p> <p>To improve a strategy you already have, choose it from the \"Improve existing\u2026\" list above the chat. \"+ New Chat\" starts again.</p> <p> </p> <p>The ActAI tab, with the notice shown the first time you use it.</p> Watch how: Generate a strategy with ActAI (1:03) <p></p> <p>What ActAI sends, and what it does not</p> <p>The first time you open ActAI it explains how your data is handled. Your prompts, the conversation, any strategy source you load and any compiler errors are sent to the configured AI provider, which handles them under its own terms. Your balances, positions and trade history are not sent, and ActAI cannot place orders. Do not paste passwords, API keys or other sensitive data into the prompt.</p> <p>Generated code is a starting point, not advice</p> <p>Code ActAI writes may be wrong, incomplete or unsuitable for live trading, and it is not financial advice. Review and back-test every strategy before running it with real money \u2014 the results are your responsibility.</p> <p>If AI features are not switched on for your account, the tab reads \"AI features aren't enabled for this account. If this is unexpected, contact your broker.\" Just after you log in it may briefly read \"Connecting to the AI service\u2026\".</p>"},{"location":"actfx/editor-tester.html","title":"Editor and Tester","text":""},{"location":"actfx/editor-tester.html#editor-and-tester","title":"Editor and Tester","text":"<p>The strategy source with the Save button and the compile-error panel beneath.</p> <p>The Editor holds the strategy source with a Save button (Ctrl+S) and a compile error panel beneath. Press Compile on the toolbar (or F9) to check the code. Errors read \"3 error(s) \u2014 click a row or press Enter to jump to the line.\"; with none it reads \"No errors.\"</p> <p>The Tester back-tests a strategy against past prices. Pick the strategy, timeframe and Speed on the toolbar, set the Balance, Spread and Slippage (in pips), choose the Symbols and the Period, adjust the strategy's parameters if you wish (Reset defaults puts them back), then press Run Test. \"Skip to results\" jumps straight to the end of a running test, and New Test clears the results.</p> <p>The Tester uses your broker's real price history where it can. If none is available for a symbol, it falls back to made-up (synthetic) prices: that symbol is marked SIM, and the finish message says \"synthetic data\". Results on synthetic prices do not tell you how the strategy would really have done.</p> <p>Results appear as eight figures \u2014 Net P/L, Profit Factor, Win Rate, Max Drawdown, Trades, Avg Win, Avg Loss and Balance \u2014 with Price, Equity and Drawdown charts, and Stats, Positions, History and Logs tabs beneath. When you test several symbols, a symbol drop-down with \u2039 and \u203a buttons switches the charts and history between them.</p> <p> </p> <p>The back-test toolbar: strategy, timeframe, speed, balance, spread and slippage, with the symbols and period beneath.</p> Watch how: Test a strategy on past prices (1:22) <p></p>"},{"location":"actfx/library.html","title":"The Strategy Library","text":""},{"location":"actfx/library.html#the-strategy-library","title":"The Strategy Library","text":"<p>The left pane lists your strategies in up to three folders:</p> Folder What is in it Running A strategy supplied by ActTrader that is still running. Shown only while it runs. Purchased Paid strategies you bought, rented or are trying (see Paid Strategies). You can run and test them, but not edit them. My Strategies Strategies you created, imported, copied or added from the Marketplace. <p>Columns are a star for favourites, Name, and Description. Click the star to mark a favourite. Searching shows a single flat list of matches.</p> <p>A running strategy shows its name in green with a \"live\" badge (\"2\u00d7 live\" when it runs more than once). With one instance running you get Stop and Pause buttons on its row (Pause changes to Resume while it is paused); with several, a scrollable strip of chips \u2014 one per instance, showing its symbol and timeframe \u2014 each with its own pause and stop button. Click a chip to open that instance's details.</p> <p> </p> <p>Right-click a strategy for Run, Test, Edit, Rename, Make a Copy, Publish to Marketplace, Improve with ActAI and Delete.</p> Watch how: Your strategy library and the Editor (1:06) <p></p>"},{"location":"actfx/library.html#getting-a-strategy","title":"Getting a strategy","text":"<ul> <li>From the Marketplace: open the Marketplace tab, pick a free strategy and click Add to My Strategies (see Adding Strategies). The fourteen strategies supplied by ActTrader are there.</li> <li>+ New: choose Blank, or From Template to start from a working example (MA Crossover, RSI Reversal, Bollinger Breakout or MACD Signal Cross). Give it a name and click Create. It opens in the Editor.</li> <li>ActAI: describe the strategy and let ActAI write it (see ActAI).</li> <li>Import, or MQL\u2192ActFX: bring in a strategy file or a MetaTrader expert.</li> </ul> Watch how: Publish your strategy (1:23) <p>If you have no strategies yet, the list offers Generate with ActAI, Create Blank and Import MQL4/MQL5, and a link to the Marketplace.</p> <p>Names cannot contain spaces: \"My EMA Cross\" is saved as \"MyEMACross\".</p>"},{"location":"actfx/library.html#the-right-click-menu","title":"The right-click menu","text":"<p>Right-click a strategy for Run, Test, Edit, Rename, Make a Copy, Publish to Marketplace\u2026, Improve with ActAI and Delete. For a purchased strategy only Run and Test are offered.</p> <ul> <li>Make a Copy adds a second copy to My Strategies, with \"Copy\" at the end of its name.</li> <li>Publish to Marketplace\u2026 shares it with other traders (see Publishing Your Strategies).</li> </ul> Watch how: Copy, rename or delete a strategy (0:45) <p></p> <p>When you select a strategy that is not running, the right-hand panel shows its name and description with Run, Edit, Test and Improve buttons, and a \"Create New with ActAI\" button for writing a new strategy from a description.</p> <p>Your strategies are saved to your account, so the same list appears on another computer when you log in there.</p> Key Action Ctrl+N New strategy F5 Run the selected strategy Shift+F5 Back-test the selected strategy Ctrl+E Open the selected strategy in the Editor F2 Rename the selected strategy Delete Delete the selected strategy"},{"location":"actfx/mql4-converter.html","title":"Converting MetaTrader Strategies","text":""},{"location":"actfx/mql4-converter.html#converting-metatrader-strategies","title":"Converting MetaTrader Strategies","text":"<p>The MQL\u2192ActFX button on the toolbar (or Ctrl+Shift+M) opens a converter for MetaTrader 4 and 5 files (.mq4, .mq5, .mqh). Click Select File or paste the source, give it a name, and press Convert. The result is saved into your library automatically. Conversion is a best-effort text translation \u2014 check the output compiles and behaves as you expect before trading it.</p> Watch how: Convert a MetaTrader (MQL4) expert (0:52) <p></p>"},{"location":"actfx/running.html","title":"Running and Stopping Strategies","text":""},{"location":"actfx/running.html#running-and-stopping-strategies","title":"Running and Stopping Strategies","text":"<p>Choosing Run opens the Run Strategy dialog, where you set the Account, Timeframe and Symbol. Strategies that can trade several symbols let you add more than one (up to 30), with a \u2261 button to fill them from a watchlist; the text under the Symbol box tells you how many symbols the strategy takes. Beneath that are the strategy's own Parameters, with + and \u2212 buttons for numbers. For stop loss and take profit settings, the dialog shows the broker's minimum distance for the selected symbol \u2014 for example \"Broker min: 5 pips for EURUSD\". At the foot are Risk Controls for Max Lot Size (in lots) and Max Drawdown (as a percentage), where 0 means no limit.</p> <p> </p> <p>Account, timeframe and symbols at the top, the strategy\u2019s own parameters beneath, and risk limits at the foot.</p> Watch how: Run and stop a strategy (1:18) <p></p> <p>While a strategy runs, the detail panel on the right shows its name, symbol, timeframe and status, with Edit Vars and Stop buttons, and eight tabs: Log, Open Trades, Closed Trades, Orders, Stats, ROI (%), Equity and Settings.</p> <p>Edit Vars opens the Edit Variables dialog, where you can change the symbols and parameters of a running strategy without stopping it. Press Save \u2014 changes apply on the next price tick.</p>"},{"location":"actfx/running.html#stopping-a-strategy","title":"Stopping a strategy","text":"<p>Stop opens a confirmation dialog with two tick boxes, both unticked by default:</p> <ul> <li>Close all open trades placed by this strategy</li> <li>Cancel all pending orders placed by this strategy</li> </ul> <p>Only trades and orders placed by this strategy are affected \u2014 your manual trades and other strategies' trades are left alone.</p> <p>Stopping a strategy leaves its trades open by default</p> <p>Because both boxes start unticked, stopping a strategy stops the automation but leaves any positions and pending orders it created in place. Tick the boxes if you want them cleared too.</p>"},{"location":"actfx/running.html#strategy-status-values","title":"Strategy status values","text":"Status Meaning Idle Created but not started. Starting Starting up. Running Running normally and reacting to prices. Paused Temporarily suspended. Resumes without restarting. Stopping Shutting down. Stopped Stopped cleanly \u2014 either you stopped it, or the script ended. Error Stopped because of a fault in the script or a timeout. <p>A cleanly stopped strategy is shown in red</p> <p>In this release the status colour in the detail panel is off by one: a strategy showing Stopped is coloured red as though it had failed, while a genuine Error may appear in normal colours and its error message may not be displayed. Always read the status word, not the colour.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/cautions.html","title":"Appendix C: Index of Cautions","text":""},{"location":"appendices/cautions.html#appendix-c-index-of-cautions","title":"Appendix C: Index of Cautions","text":"<p>Each point below is explained in full where you meet it in the manual. This page is a checklist, so you can confirm you have seen them all.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/cautions.html#read-these-before-you-trade","title":"Read these before you trade","text":"Caution Explained in Ordinary messages disappear on their own. Margin calls stay on screen until you dismiss them. Check Events and Messages if you step away. 11 Turning off Show notifications hides messages and sounds \u2014 only margin-call windows still appear. 11 Placing an order from the chart's Buy/Sell strip, and pressing Remove in the Stop Loss or Take Profit dialog, act on one click with no confirmation. 3.3.1, 3.4.2 Quick Trade turns every Bid and Ask cell into a live one-click order, and makes closing a position or removing an order act without asking. The Watchlist Orders placed while disconnected are submitted later as pending orders, not market orders. 11.3 \"Reset all distances to default\" cannot be undone. 10.11 A price alert fires once and is then removed from your list. 11.4"},{"location":"appendices/cautions.html#wording-that-does-not-match-behaviour","title":"Wording that does not match behaviour","text":"Caution Explained in The Open Positions column headed \"Close\" shows the current price and is not clickable, although its tooltip says \"Close this position\". Open Positions The chart layout menu labels the two-chart options the wrong way round. Chart Controls \"(Bonus : 0.00)\" on the status bar is fixed text, not a live figure. The Account Status Bar The Bonus column's tooltip reads \"Price Shift\". 8.1 The Price Alerts B/S column shows Bid or Ask. 8.5 \"Export to Excel\u2026\" produces a CSV file. Export to CSV An incomplete filter clears it instead of warning you. Filtering The message \"Offline mode \u2014 simulated prices\" means your session was lost; the prices shown are your last known prices, not simulated ones. 11.3"},{"location":"appendices/cautions.html#not-available-in-this-release","title":"Not available in this release","text":"Caution Explained in Languages other than English are only partly translated. Settings Before You Log In Chart Alerts on the Summary tab has no data behind it. 8.5 \"OCO Link\" in the pending-order menu is permanently greyed out. Pending Orders \"Organize Managed Accounts\" is permanently greyed out. 8.1 Analytics is unavailable for some managed and master accounts. 9.4 Exported files go to a temporary folder \u2014 save them if you need to keep them. Export to CSV"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html","title":"Appendix A: Message and Event Reference","text":""},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#appendix-a-message-and-event-reference","title":"Appendix A: Message and Event Reference","text":""},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#message-kinds","title":"Message kinds","text":"Kind Left bar colour On screen for Needs acknowledging? Information Your broker's accent colour (orange by default) About 4 seconds No Success Green About 4 seconds No Warning Amber About 4 seconds No Error Red About 6 seconds No Critical (margin calls on your account) Red window in the middle of the screen Until you press Dismiss or View Position Yes <p>At most seven small messages are shown at once; older ones give way to newer. An identical message repeated within two seconds is shown only once. Critical windows are not counted in the seven and never disappear by themselves.</p> <p>When Show notifications is off (Settings \u2192 Trading), the small messages are not shown at all. Critical windows are still shown.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#complete-message-list","title":"Complete message list","text":"<p>Everything the application can tell you, grouped by kind. Values in angle brackets are filled in at the time. Where a message has a second line, it is shown after a dash (\u2014).</p>"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#critical-stays-on-screen-until-you-dismiss-it","title":"Critical (stays on screen until you dismiss it)","text":"Message When Margin Call for Account  \u2014 Margin Call Level 1!\u2026 Equity has fallen below used margin Margin Call for Account  \u2014 Margin Call Overdue!\u2026 The margin-call grace period expired Margin Call for Account  \u2014 MC Levels: Hedge All\u2026 Positions were hedged automatically Margin Call for Account  \u2014 MC Levels: Close All \u2014 All open postions are closed! The most severe margin call. Every position was closed. (The spelling is as shipped) Margin Call for Account  \u2014 Margin Call!\u2026 Some positions will be closed Margin Call for Account  \u2014 Margin Call released!\u2026 The account recovered Short Margin for Account  \u2014 Short Margin!\u2026 Balance has fallen below used margin Short Margin for Account  \u2014 Short Margin Overdue!\u2026 The short-margin period expired Margin Call on account #. The following open positions are closed:\u2026 Your broker closed positions. The full list follows"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#success","title":"Success","text":"Message When Buy   @  A market order placed from the chart strip or Living Market was accepted Sell   @  As above, for a sell Order placed \u2014 # An order was accepted Order placed An order was accepted but the broker returned no reference Position # closed A position was closed Position closed A position was closed with no reference returned Order Executed \u2014 Buy  An order was filled and a position opened. Size, price and trade number appear beneath Connected \u2014 live prices Reconnected after an interruption Feed restored \u2014  queued order(s) submitted as pending Held orders were sent after an outage Exported  rows to CSV An export succeeded. The file path appears beneath Template saved A chart template was saved Account added successfully A new account was added Account removed An account's stored credentials were deleted Password changed Your password was changed Updated  instrument(s) A bulk order-distance change was applied Copy made Make a Copy added a second copy of a strategy to My Strategies Added to My Strategies A Marketplace strategy was added to ActFX Published Your strategy is live in the Marketplace Reported Your report on a Marketplace strategy was sent Report taken back You withdrew a report Back-test complete A back-test finished. A summary appears beneath (shown as a warning if some symbols failed)"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#information","title":"Information","text":"Message When Order cancelled A pending order was removed Stop loss updated A stop-loss was changed by dragging it on the chart Take profit updated A take-profit was changed by dragging it on the chart Order rate updated A pending order's trigger price was changed by dragging Order modified An order, stop or limit was changed from a dialog Chart setup updated on another device Your chart settings changed elsewhere. Switch instrument or reopen the chart to load them Alt+E \u2014 focus a list first Alt+E was pressed on the Summary tab with no table selected Action cancelled A voice instruction was cancelled at the confirmation step Charts off \u2014  chart window(s) closed You switched charts off and open chart windows were closed Version  is available A newer version can be downloaded from Help on the right-hand strip User manual coming soon F1 or a manual link was used where your broker's manual is not yet available"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#warning","title":"Warning","text":"Message When Offline mode \u2014 simulated prices Your session was lost and the application is logging you back in; prices are not live No Feed:   lots queued \u2014 will submit when feed restores An order was placed while disconnected and is being held Price Alert: The   rate has reached  A price alert triggered Price alerts are unavailable: the broker's alert server could not be reached. Your price alerts could not be loaded Account . Equity has reached <p>% of Used Margin.</p> Early equity warning Account . Equity has reached the minimum. Equity is at the account minimum Closed trades could not be loaded The Closed tab's history request failed. The reason appears beneath Chart window limit reached You already have the maximum number of chart windows open No rows updated (checked rows' broker minimum exceeds the value). A bulk distance change matched nothing Not saved \u2014 broker minimum is  pips for this instrument A distance below the broker's minimum was rejected Symbol limit reached A strategy already watches the maximum number of symbols Watchlist is empty You tried to fill a strategy's symbols from a watchlist with no instruments Watch list limited to  symbols Only the first symbols of a watchlist were added to a strategy Chart symbol unchanged A running strategy's first (chart) symbol cannot change until you stop and run it again"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#error","title":"Error","text":"Message When Order failed An order was rejected. The reason appears beneath (see below) Wrong Account Type or Username or Password Login credentials were not accepted This broker's server rejected the login due to a server-side error\u2026 A fault on your broker's server Login failed \u2014 the server returned an unexpected response\u2026 The login reply could not be understood Order failed \u2014 No instrument selected \u2014 select a symbol first A chart trade with no instrument loaded Order failed \u2014 No live price for  A chart trade with no price available Invalid price \u2014 Chart produced an invalid price value \u2014 drag cancelled A dragged level was not usable Order not found \u2014 Order # may have been filled or cancelled The dragged order no longer exists Position not found \u2014 Position # may have already been closed The dragged position no longer exists Unsupported chart action \u2014 This chart action isn't recognized \u2014 please use the position/order panel instead The chart sent an action the application does not handle Invalid lot size The trade size in the chart strip was zero or unusable No live price for  A chart-strip or Living Market trade was attempted with no price No instrument selected A chart-strip trade was attempted with no instrument  is not available on this broker A Living Market instrument your broker does not offer Cannot resolve instrument id for  A Living Market instrument could not be matched to your broker's list The price alert could not be saved. Your broker did not accept a price alert. Any reason is added after a colon Price alerts are not available right now. An alert was added or changed while the alert service was unavailable Unknown instrument  A price alert's instrument could not be matched Export failed A CSV export could not be written. The reason appears beneath Password change failed Your broker rejected the password change Action failed A voice instruction could not be carried out Copy failed A copy of a strategy could not be created Not added A Marketplace strategy could not be added. The reason appears beneath Cannot test it A paid strategy could not be opened in the Tester. The reason appears beneath Not done A Marketplace action (trial, request, report) did not go through. The reason appears beneath Back-test failed A back-test failed for every symbol <p>ActAI and the Reports tab also show messages headed \"ActAI Generator\" or with the text the report page reported \u2014 these describe what happened in that panel.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#reasons-shown-beneath-order-failed","title":"Reasons shown beneath \"Order failed\"","text":"<p>Besides your broker's own wording, you may see:</p> Reason Meaning The amount must be not less than  and not more than  lots The size is outside the instrument's limits The amount must be a multiple of Trade Step. Trade Step on  is  lots The size is not a whole number of steps Rate must be at least  pips from the current market price A pending order or stop/limit is too close to the market Buy Limit must be below Ask / Buy Stop must be above Ask / Sell Limit must be above Bid / Sell Stop must be below Bid The entry price is on the wrong side of the market Stop Loss for a Buy position must be below the current market () And the matching messages for Sell positions and Take Profit Trailing distance must be at least  pips The trailing stop is too tight  position(s) could not be closed \u2014 no live price for . Close them individually or try again. A bulk close skipped positions with no current price Session expired \u2014 reconnecting\u2026 Your session ended; the application is logging you back in Server did not respond in time \u2014 please try again The broker did not answer This is a read-only (customer) account. Trading actions are not permitted. Your account can view but not trade Account not ready \u2014 the server has not returned a numeric account ID\u2026 Your account details have not loaded yet Rate limit: too many order requests per second \u2014 this request was rejected\u2026 A strategy sent orders too quickly"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#quick-trade-notes-inside-the-watchlist","title":"Quick Trade notes inside the watchlist","text":"<p>With Quick Trade on, these appear briefly inside the watchlist rather than in the corner:</p> Note When Buy  placed / Sell  placed A one-click order was accepted No price available for  There is no current price to trade at Invalid lot size for  The size in the row is zero or unusable The amount must be not less than  and not more than  lots The size is outside the instrument's limits Order failed, or your broker's reason The order was rejected"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#events-and-messages-log","title":"Events and Messages log","text":"<p>Trading, margin and connection messages above are also recorded on the Summary tab, along with entries that appear only in the log. Login errors are not recorded \u2014 they stay on the login screen. The Source column tells you where an entry came from:</p> Source Meaning Your trader ID An action you took Strategy:  An action taken by that ActFX strategy Leader:  A position copied from that leader Information Login, logout and connection events SYSTEM Generated by your broker's server EXCEPTION An error or a rejected order Warning An equity or margin-call notice <p>Entry formats:</p> Log entry Meaning Order Placed: #  An order was accepted Order Cancelled: #  An order was removed Order Triggered: #  A pending order's price was reached Position Opened: Ticket #  A position opened. Time, side, instrument, size and price follow Position Closed: Ticket #  A position closed. Side, instrument, size and opening price follow Your  order # to   lot at  was executed at  A conditional order filled Trader  has logged on from . A login was recorded Duplicate logon using your user ID from  Your credentials were used to log in elsewhere Trader  has logged off. A logout was recorded Login You connected Logged out You disconnected <p>The log holds the most recent 2,000 entries and is kept between sessions.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/messages.html#sound-events","title":"Sound events","text":"<p>Each event below plays its own short sound. You can switch each one on or off, and set the volume, in Settings \u2192 Trading. No sound plays while Show notifications is off.</p> Event Plays when Order placed An order is accepted Order filled A new position opens \u2014 a market order, or a pending order whose price was reached Position closed A position closes Order rejected / failed An order is refused Price alert triggered An alert fires Margin call A margin-call message arrives for the account, including \"Margin Call released\". Equity warnings do not play a sound Feed / connection lost The price feed drops"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html","title":"Appendix B: Keyboard Shortcut Reference","text":""},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#appendix-b-keyboard-shortcut-reference","title":"Appendix B: Keyboard Shortcut Reference","text":"<p>Press Shift+F1 in the application for this list on screen. Shortcuts tied to a panel work only while that panel has focus. None of the shortcuts in B.1 to B.6 work while a dialog is open \u2014 except Ctrl+K, which opens or closes the command palette at any time. On macOS, Ctrl appears as \u2318 and Alt as \u2325.</p> Watch how: Use keyboard shortcuts (0:45) <p></p>"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#general","title":"General","text":"Shortcut Action Where F5 Refresh current panel. Tables already update by themselves, so you will normally see no change Anywhere F11 Toggle full-screen window Anywhere Escape Exit full-screen window (only while full-screen). If the chart has an edit in progress, the first press cancels that edit Anywhere F1 Open Trader Manual Anywhere Shift+F1 Show keyboard shortcuts Anywhere Alt+Q Toggle Quick Trade mode Anywhere Ctrl+Shift+Tab Switch to next workspace tab Anywhere Ctrl+Shift+Backtab Switch to previous workspace tab Anywhere Ctrl+K Open or close the command palette Anywhere, even with a dialog open Space Open the voice command panel Anywhere while logged in, except when typing in a text field Ctrl+A Select all rows Open Positions, Pending Orders"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#instruments-and-watchlist","title":"Instruments and watchlist","text":"Shortcut Action Where Alt+B Buy selected instrument (at the Ask) Watchlist, Instruments Alt+S Sell selected instrument (at the Bid) Watchlist, Instruments Alt+N Open chart for selected instrument Watchlist, Instruments Alt+P Create price alert Watchlist, Instruments Alt+F Focus the search field Anywhere Alt+W Toggle the News panel Instruments"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#open-positions","title":"Open positions","text":"Shortcut Action Alt+C  (also Ctrl+W, Ctrl+C, Delete) Close selected position \u2014 opens the Close Position window (closes at once if Quick Trade is on). With more than one selected, asks you to confirm closing them all (again, at once if Quick Trade is on) Alt+H  (also Ctrl+H) Hedge selected position Alt+T Set or change the Stop Loss Alt+L Set or change the Take Profit Alt+E Export open positions to CSV"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#pending-orders","title":"Pending orders","text":"Shortcut Action Alt+M  (also Ctrl+M) Modify selected order Alt+R  (also Ctrl+R, Delete) Cancel selected order \u2014 or all selected, if more than one. Asks you to confirm first Alt+E Export pending orders to CSV"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#closed-positions-and-summary","title":"Closed positions and Summary","text":"Shortcut Action Where Ctrl+C Copy selected Trade ID to the clipboard Closed Positions Alt+E Export closed trades to CSV Closed Positions Alt+E Export the focused list to CSV Summary <p>Every Alt+E export first shows an Export to CSV window describing what will be saved; press Export to create the file.</p>"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#actfx","title":"ActFX","text":"Shortcut Action F9 Compile strategy (Editor) F5 Run selected strategy Shift+F5 Back-test selected strategy Ctrl+E Edit selected strategy in the editor Delete Delete selected strategy Ctrl+Shift+M Open the MQL4 \u2192 ActFX converter Ctrl+S Save the strategy open in the Editor"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#inside-the-deal-ticket","title":"Inside the Deal Ticket","text":"Shortcut Action Ctrl+Tab Cycle order type: Market \u2192 Limit \u2192 Entry \u2192 OCO Alt+B Switch to Buy (not available when hedging a Buy position) Alt+S Switch to Sell (not available when hedging a Sell position) Up / Down Step the value in the focused numeric field Enter Submit the order Escape Close without placing"},{"location":"appendices/shortcuts.html#moving-around","title":"Moving around","text":"Key Action Tab / Shift+Tab Move between the areas of the current tab. Landing on a tab button also switches to it Up / Down Move through a list. Lists wrap from the last row to the first Shift+Up / Shift+Down Extend a selection (Open Positions) Home / End Jump to the first or last row Left / Right Move between adjacent tabs and switch to them Enter Act on the highlighted row Escape Close a dialog, clear a search, or collapse a multiple selection Menu key Open the right-click menu for the highlighted row"},{"location":"appendices/support.html","title":"Appendix D: Support","text":""},{"location":"appendices/support.html#appendix-d-support","title":"Appendix D: Support","text":""},{"location":"appendices/support.html#contacting-your-broker","title":"Contacting your broker","text":"<p>Your broker is responsible for your account, your credentials, the instruments offered, margin requirements, commissions and report access. Contact them for:</p> <ul> <li>Login problems that mention a server error</li> <li>Rejected orders where the reason comes from the server</li> <li>Margin, commission and rollover questions</li> <li>Missing instruments or missing reports</li> <li>Analytics not being available for your account</li> </ul> Detail Your broker's information Broker name Support email Support telephone Support hours Account number Server"},{"location":"appendices/support.html#before-you-make-contact","title":"Before you make contact","text":"<p>Having these to hand will speed things up:</p> <ol> <li>The exact wording of any message, and the time it appeared.</li> <li>Your account identifier and the server you connect to \u2014 both are on the Settings \u2192 Account tab.</li> <li>The instrument, size and direction of any trade involved.</li> <li>The Trade ID or Order reference, if there is one.</li> <li>A diagnostic report \u2014 Settings \u2192 Diagnostics collects system information, network tests and logs, and can save them to a file to attach.</li> </ol> Watch how: Send a diagnostic report (0:36) <p></p>"},{"location":"appendices/support.html#in-application-help","title":"In-application help","text":"Where What it gives you F1 Your broker's trader manual, in your browser. If your broker's manual is not ready yet, you see \"User manual coming soon\" Shift+F1 The keyboard shortcut list Ctrl+K The command palette, for opening charts, tabs and other actions by typing The ? button on a tab A guided tour of that tab. Available on every tab except Reports Help on the right strip The manual, the shortcut list, and Check for updates (or Download, when a newer version is available) Settings \u2192 Diagnostics Collects information for support"},{"location":"appendices/support.html#about-this-manual","title":"About this manual","text":"<p>This manual describes the Trader interface of ActTrader v2.0. It was produced by auditing the shipped application source, so every screen, column, control, menu item and message described here exists in the product, with labels reproduced as they appear on screen.</p> <p>Section headings and figure numbers are stable, so you can quote them when reporting a problem or asking a question.</p>"},{"location":"charts/index.html","title":"Working with Charts","text":""},{"location":"charts/index.html#working-with-charts","title":"Working with Charts","text":"<p>The chart is where most traders spend their time. As well as showing price history, it draws your open positions and pending orders directly on the price axis, so you can manage them without leaving the chart.</p> <p> </p> <p>A single chart showing the toolbar along the top, the drawing-tool bar down the left edge, the date-range buttons along the bottom, the price axis on the right, and an open position drawn as a horizontal line.</p> Watch how: Read the chart (0:52) <p></p> <p>Turning the charts off</p> <p>The \u25a6 button at the top of the Trading tab turns all charts off, which frees up memory and processing power. Press it again to turn the charts back on.</p>"},{"location":"charts/index.html#in-this-section","title":"In this section","text":"Page What the Chart Shows Instrument, timeframe, date range, go to a date, price scale, chart style and Bar Replay Indicators Add, change and remove indicators; indicator templates Drawing Tools Cursors, trend lines, Fibonacci, icons and more Trading from the Chart Your trades on the chart; set SL/TP; place and close orders Layout and Appearance Several charts, Chart Settings, Bid/Ask lines and the side panel Charts in Their Own Window Separate chart windows"},{"location":"charts/chart-windows.html","title":"Charts in Their Own Window","text":""},{"location":"charts/chart-windows.html#charts-in-their-own-window","title":"Charts in Their Own Window","text":"<p>Press New chart at the top of the Trading tab to open the current instrument in its own window, which you can move anywhere, even onto a second monitor. Right-click inside any chart and choose Undock this chart to do the same for a chart already on screen.</p> <p>Each chart window works on its own: changing its instrument does not change your other charts.</p> <p>The buttons at the right of the window's title bar minimise it, make it full size (and restore it), and close it (X).</p> <p>You can have up to six chart windows open at once. When you reach the limit, New chart and Undock this chart are greyed out and the New chart button shows \"Chart window limit reached (6)\".</p> Watch how: Pop out charts and panels (0:40) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/drawing-tools.html","title":"Drawing Tools","text":""},{"location":"charts/drawing-tools.html#drawing-tools","title":"Drawing Tools","text":"<p>The toolbar down the left edge of the chart holds the drawing tools. The pencil button (Drawing Tools) on the chart toolbar shows or hides it. Each button on the bar opens a group of tools. Pick a tool, then click on the chart where the drawing starts and click again where it ends.</p> <p>Click an existing drawing to select it. A small bar appears above it where you can change its colour, line width and line style; drag its handles to reshape it. Press Delete (or Backspace) to remove the selected drawing. For text drawings, double-click to edit the text.</p> <p> </p> <p>The vertical toolbar at the left of the chart, with one tool group open to show the tools inside it.</p> Watch how: Draw on the chart (0:48) <p></p> Group Tools Trend Lines &amp; Channels Trend Line \u00b7 Ray \u00b7 Info Line \u00b7 Extended Line \u00b7 Trend Angle \u00b7 Horizontal Line \u00b7 Horizontal Ray \u00b7 Vertical Line \u00b7 Cross Line \u00b7 Parallel Channel \u00b7 Disjoint Channel \u00b7 Flat Top/Bottom Channel Fibonacci &amp; Gann Tools Fibonacci Retracement \u00b7 Fibonacci Extension \u00b7 Fibonacci Channel \u00b7 Fibonacci Timezone \u00b7 Trend-Based Fib Time \u00b7 Fib Speed Resistance Arcs \u00b7 Fib Wedge \u00b7 Fibonacci Circles \u00b7 Fibonacci Spiral \u00b7 Fibonacci Speed Resistance Fan \u00b7 Gann Fan \u00b7 Gann Square \u00b7 Gann Square Fixed \u00b7 Gann Box Geometric Shapes Rectangle \u00b7 Rotated Rectangle \u00b7 Ellipse \u00b7 Triangle \u00b7 Circle \u00b7 Arc \u00b7 Curve \u00b7 Double Curve \u00b7 Polyline \u00b7 Path Measurement Tools Price Range \u00b7 Date Range \u00b7 Date &amp; Price Range \u00b7 Ruler Pitchfork Tools Pitchfork \u00b7 Schiff Pitchfork \u00b7 Modified Schiff Pitchfork \u00b7 Inside Pitchfork \u00b7 Pitchfan Volume &amp; Statistical Tools Fixed Range Volume Profile \u00b7 Anchored Volume Profile \u00b7 Anchored VWAP \u00b7 Volume Profile \u00b7 Regression Trend Icons Emoji and symbols in several sets, to mark a point on the chart Annotation Tools Text \u00b7 Callout \u00b7 Price Label \u00b7 Arrow \u00b7 Flag \u00b7 Price Note \u00b7 Anchored Note \u00b7 Anchored Text \u00b7 Note \u00b7 Pin \u00b7 Table \u00b7 Comment \u00b7 Signpost \u00b7 Arrow Up \u00b7 Arrow Down \u00b7 Arrow Mark Left \u00b7 Arrow Mark Right Pattern Recognition Head &amp; Shoulders \u00b7 Triangle Pattern \u00b7 3 Drives Pattern \u00b7 ABCD Pattern \u00b7 Cypher Pattern \u00b7 Butterfly Pattern \u00b7 Bat Pattern \u00b7 XABCD Pattern \u00b7 Gartley Pattern \u00b7 Crab Pattern \u00b7 Shark Pattern Elliott Wave Tools Elliott Impulse (12345) \u00b7 Elliott Corrective (ABC) \u00b7 Elliott Wave Triangle \u00b7 Elliott Wave Combination \u00b7 Elliott Triple Combo (WXYXZ) \u00b7 Elliott Double Three (WXY) Brush &amp; Highlighter Brush \u00b7 Highlighter Advanced Tools Ghost Feed \u00b7 Projection \u00b7 Sine Line \u00b7 Cyclic Lines \u00b7 Time Cycles"},{"location":"charts/drawing-tools.html#cursor","title":"Cursor","text":"<p>The top button of the drawing bar sets how the mouse pointer looks and behaves on the chart:</p> Cursor What it does Cross The default crosshair, with the price and time on the axes. Dot A small dot instead of the crosshair. Arrow An ordinary arrow pointer. Demonstration Draws a trail that fades away, handy when you show the chart to someone. Eraser Click a drawing to delete it. Zoom In Drag over an area to zoom in on it. <p> </p> <p>The top button of the drawing bar open, listing Cross, Dot, Arrow, Demonstration, Eraser and Zoom In.</p> Watch how: Cursors, icons and the side panel (0:52) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/drawing-tools.html#actions-menu","title":"Actions menu","text":"<p>The Actions button (\u2026) at the top of the drawing bar opens a short menu. These commands apply to the drawings on that chart:</p> Command Effect Shortcut Undo Reverse the last change. Ctrl+Z Redo Reapply a change you undid. \u2014 Delete Selected Remove the drawing you have selected. Delete or Backspace Clear All Remove every drawing from this chart. \u2014 Hide All Hide the drawings without deleting them. Press it again (Show All) to bring them back. \u2014 Lock All Prevent drawings from being moved by accident. Press it again (Unlock All) to release them. \u2014 Magnet Mode Snaps the points of a drawing to the nearest candle's open, high, low or close. \u2014 Keep Drawing Mode Keeps the tool selected after a drawing, so you can draw several in a row. \u2014 Copy to All Charts Copies the drawings on this chart to your other charts. \u2014 Hide Drawings Toolbar Hides the drawing bar. The pencil on the chart toolbar shows it again. \u2014 <p>Your drawings are saved</p> <p>Drawings are remembered per instrument, so returning to an instrument brings back the analysis you left on it. Indicators stay with the chart when you change instrument; save a set you use often as an indicator template (see Indicators).</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html","title":"Indicators","text":""},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#indicators","title":"Indicators","text":"<p>Press the Indicators button on the chart toolbar to add a study. More than a hundred are built in. They are listed in groups, and the search box at the top finds one by typing part of its name. Click an indicator to add it to the chart straight away. The button then shows how many you have, for example \"Indicators (2)\".</p> <p> </p> <p>The Indicators drop-down open on the chart, with the search box at the top and the indicators listed under their group headings.</p> Watch how: Add indicators (0:40) <p></p> <p>Most indicators can be added more than once with different settings \u2014 two moving averages of different lengths, for example. A few can only be added once: Volume, On Balance Volume, Accumulation/Distribution, Awesome Oscillator, Volume Weighted Average Price, Ichimoku Cloud, Parabolic SAR and Pivot Points Standard.</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#trend","title":"Trend","text":"<p>Moving Average (MA) \u00b7 Exponential Moving Average (EMA) \u00b7 Weighted Moving Average (WMA) \u00b7 Hull Moving Average (HMA) \u00b7 Moving Average Ribbon (MARibbon) \u00b7 Supertrend \u00b7 Parabolic SAR (PSAR) \u00b7 Ichimoku Cloud (Ichimoku) \u00b7 Linear Regression (LinReg) \u00b7 Arnaud Legoux Moving Average (ALMA) \u00b7 Double EMA (DEMA) \u00b7 Triple EMA (TEMA) \u00b7 Least Squares Moving Average (LSMA) \u00b7 McGinley Dynamic \u00b7 Smoothed Moving Average (SMMA) \u00b7 Volume Weighted Moving Average (VWMA) \u00b7 Moving Average Hamming \u00b7 Moving Average Adaptive (AMA) \u00b7 Moving Average Channel \u00b7 Moving Average Double \u00b7 Moving Average Triple \u00b7 Moving Average Multiple \u00b7 Guppy Multiple Moving Average \u00b7 Williams Alligator \u00b7 Zig Zag \u00b7 MA Cross \u00b7 EMA Cross \u00b7 MA with EMA Cross</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#volatility","title":"Volatility","text":"<p>Bollinger Bands (BB) \u00b7 Keltner Channels (KC) \u00b7 Donchian Channels (DC) \u00b7 Average True Range (ATR) \u00b7 Mass Index \u00b7 Relative Volatility Index (RVI) \u00b7 Chaikin Volatility \u00b7 Bollinger Bands %B \u00b7 Bollinger Bands Width \u00b7 Historical Volatility \u00b7 Volatility Close-to-Close \u00b7 Volatility Zero Trend Close-to-Close \u00b7 Volatility O-H-L-C \u00b7 Volatility Index \u00b7 Standard Deviation \u00b7 Standard Error \u00b7 Standard Error Bands \u00b7 Choppiness Index \u00b7 Chop Zone \u00b7 Envelopes \u00b7 Price Channel \u00b7 Chande Kroll Stop</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#momentum","title":"Momentum","text":"<p>Relative Strength Index (RSI) \u00b7 Stochastic Oscillator (Stoch) \u00b7 Stochastic RSI (StochRSI) \u00b7 MACD \u00b7 Commodity Channel Index (CCI) \u00b7 Williams %R (%R) \u00b7 Rate of Change (ROC) \u00b7 Awesome Oscillator (AO) \u00b7 Accelerator Oscillator (AC) \u00b7 Accumulative Swing Index (ASI) \u00b7 Balance of Power (BOP) \u00b7 Chande Momentum Oscillator (CMO) \u00b7 Connors RSI (CRSI) \u00b7 Coppock Curve \u00b7 Detrended Price Oscillator (DPO) \u00b7 Fisher Transform \u00b7 Know Sure Thing (KST) \u00b7 Majority Rule \u00b7 Momentum \u00b7 Price Oscillator (PPO) \u00b7 Relative Vigor Index (RVGI) \u00b7 SMI Ergodic Indicator \u00b7 TRIX \u00b7 True Strength Index (TSI) \u00b7 Ultimate Oscillator (UO) \u00b7 Rank Correlation Index (RCI) \u00b7 Correlation Coefficient \u00b7 Correlation - Log</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#volume","title":"Volume","text":"<p>On Balance Volume (OBV) \u00b7 Volume (VOL) \u00b7 Volume Weighted Average Price (VWAP) \u00b7 Accumulation/Distribution (A/D) \u00b7 Money Flow Index (MFI) \u00b7 Chaikin Money Flow (CMF) \u00b7 Ease of Movement (EOM) \u00b7 Elder's Force Index (EFI) \u00b7 Klinger Oscillator (KVO) \u00b7 Volume Oscillator \u00b7 Net Volume \u00b7 Price Volume Trend (PVT) \u00b7 Chaikin Oscillator \u00b7 Advance/Decline \u00b7 Volume Profile Visible Range (VPVR)</p> <p>The volume indicators are greyed out when the chart has no volume data for the instrument.</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#supportresistance","title":"Support/Resistance","text":"<p>Pivot Points Standard (Pivot) \u00b7 Fibonacci Retracement (Fib) \u00b7 52 Week High/Low \u00b7 Williams Fractal</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#trend-strength","title":"Trend Strength","text":"<p>ADX \u00b7 Aroon \u00b7 Directional Movement (DMI) \u00b7 Vortex Indicator \u00b7 Trend Strength Index \u00b7 Linear Regression Slope</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#price-transformation","title":"Price Transformation","text":"<p>Average Price \u00b7 Median Price \u00b7 Typical Price \u00b7 Ratio \u00b7 Spread</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#changing-or-removing-an-indicator","title":"Changing or removing an indicator","text":"<p>Each indicator you add gets a small tag at the top of the chart:</p> Button What it does Gear Opens the indicator's settings \u2014 for example its period, colour, the price it uses and its timeframe. Click Update to apply your changes. Eye Hides the indicator for a moment. Click it again to show it. X Removes the indicator from the chart. <p>Colour boxes in the settings open a colour palette: click a colour, or type a colour code (for example #2962FF) and press OK.</p> <p> </p> <p>The settings window for a Moving Average, with the Period field and the Update button.</p> Watch how: Change indicator settings (0:44) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#indicators-stay-with-the-chart","title":"Indicators stay with the chart","text":"<p>Indicators belong to the chart, not to the instrument. When you pick another instrument, the same indicators, with the same settings, are drawn on it. Drawings, the timeframe and the view are still kept for each instrument.</p>"},{"location":"charts/indicators.html#indicator-templates","title":"Indicator templates","text":"<p>A template saves the set of indicators on a chart, so you can put the same set on any chart later.</p> <ol> <li>Add the indicators you want, with their settings.</li> <li>Open Indicators and scroll to Templates at the bottom of the list.</li> <li>Click Save current indicators\u2026, type a name and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>To use a template, open Indicators and click its name under Templates. It replaces the indicators on that chart. The X next to a template deletes it. Templates are saved with your profile and can be used on every chart, including charts in their own window.</p> <p> </p> <p>The bottom of the Indicators list, with a saved template and Save current indicators.</p> Watch how: Indicator templates (1:15) <p></p> <p>Pivot Points appear in two places</p> <p>The Pivot Points Standard indicator draws levels on the chart itself. The Instruments tab also has a pivot strip showing the same kind of levels as a bar with the current price marked \u2014 see 7.4. Use whichever suits you.</p>"},{"location":"charts/layout-and-appearance.html","title":"Layout and Appearance","text":""},{"location":"charts/layout-and-appearance.html#layout-and-appearance","title":"Layout and Appearance","text":"Control Where What it does New chart Top of the Trading tab Opens a chart in its own window. See 6.6. Linked Top of the Trading tab When on, every chart follows your watchlist selection. When off, only the active chart changes. See Chart Controls. Layout picker Top of the Trading tab Shows 1, 2, 4, 6 or 9 charts at once: a single chart, 2 side by side, 2 stacked, a 2\u00d72 grid, a 2\u00d73 grid or a 3\u00d73 grid. See Chart Controls. \u25a6 Top of the Trading tab Turns all charts off, and on again. Settings (gear) Chart toolbar Opens Chart Settings \u2014 see below. Toggle Fullscreen Chart toolbar Expands the chart to fill the screen. Press it again (Exit Fullscreen) to return. Chart bottom bar Panels icon on the right-hand strip Shows or hides the date-range buttons under the chart. Undock this chart Right-click the chart Moves the chart into its own window. See 6.6. Trade from Charts Chart toolbar, right of the gear Turns trading from the chart on and off. When off, your position and order lines are hidden. See 6.4. Side panel The small buttons at the right edge of the chart Opens the Data Window and Objects panel \u2014 see below. <p>When the window is narrow, New chart, Linked and the layout picker move into a drawer. Click the \u2039 button near the right end of the tab bar (its tooltip reads \"Chart controls\") to open it.</p> Watch how: More chart controls (0:44) <p></p> Watch how: Show several charts at once (1:08) <p></p> Watch how: Use the settings icons (1:27) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/layout-and-appearance.html#chart-settings","title":"Chart Settings","text":"<p>Click the gear on the chart toolbar to open Chart Settings. It has five pages:</p> Page What you can set Appearance The chart colours: Background, Grid, Axis Text, Axis Border, Crosshair, and the Candle Body, Candle Wick and Candle Border colours for rising and falling candles, plus Volume, and how bars are coloured. Click a colour box to open the palette: pick a colour, or type a colour code (for example #080808) and press OK. Status Line What shows next to the instrument name at the top left: the instrument name, the open/high/low/close of the candle under the cursor, the bar change and the volume. Scales The tags on the price scale: Last price, Bid, Ask, and High and low. This is where you switch the Bid and Ask price lines on or off. Time-axis countdown shows how long until the current candle closes. Canvas Horizontal and vertical grid lines, and a large faint watermark behind the chart (the instrument name, or your own text, in the size you choose). Trading Show picks which trade lines appear: All, Positions Only, Orders Only or None. Position Style draws each open position as a Full Line or a Dot. Always show SL/TP keeps stop-loss and take-profit lines visible. <p>At the bottom of the window:</p> Control What it does Templates\u2026 Puts a saved settings template on this chart. Save\u2026 Saves the current settings as a template, under a name. Apply to all charts When ticked, your changes go to every chart, not just this one. Reset to Defaults Goes back to the standard settings. <p>A theme picked in Chart Settings changes the whole app, just like the Theme icon on the right-hand strip. The chart's time zone always follows the app's time zone setting (Settings \u2192 Account).</p> <p> </p> <p>The Appearance page with the colour palette open on the Background colour.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Scales page with the Last price, Bid, Ask and High and low switches.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Chart Settings window open on the Trading page, showing Show, Position Style and Always show SL/TP.</p> Watch how: Chart settings and colours (1:01) <p></p> <p>Light or dark charts</p> <p>The charts follow the app's theme. Use the Theme icon on the right-hand strip to switch between dark and light.</p>"},{"location":"charts/layout-and-appearance.html#the-side-panel","title":"The side panel","text":"<p>The small buttons at the right edge of the chart open a side panel with two tabs:</p> Tab What it shows Data Window The date, open, high, low, close, change and volume of the candle under the cursor, and the values of your indicators. Objects The drawings on this chart. <p>Close it with its X. The panel starts closed, and each chart remembers whether its panel is open.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Data Window tab open at the right of the chart, showing the values of the candle under the cursor.</p> Watch how: Cursors, icons and the side panel (0:52) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html","title":"Trading from the Chart","text":""},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#trading-from-the-chart","title":"Trading from the Chart","text":"<p>Your open positions and pending orders are drawn on the chart as horizontal lines at their prices, so you can see them against the market at a glance.</p> <p> </p> <p>A position with its stop-loss (SL) and take-profit (TP). Each label shows the price and what it is worth if reached.</p> Watch how: Move stop loss / take profit on the chart (0:41) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#reading-the-lines","title":"Reading the lines","text":"Line What it is Its label shows Position line An open position. Side and size, for example \"Buy 0.01\", with the live profit or loss. Order line A pending order waiting for its price. Side and size, for example \"Sell 0.10\". SL line The stop-loss attached to a position or order. \"SL\", the price, and the loss if it is reached. TP line The take-profit attached to a position or order. \"TP\", the price, and the profit if it is reached. <p>Stop-loss and take-profit lines are shown all the time. You can change what the chart shows from the gear on the chart toolbar (Chart Settings), on the Trading page \u2014 see 6.5.</p> <p>Levels at similar prices are grouped</p> <p>When two or more positions or orders sit at almost the same price, the chart combines their labels into one badge \u2014 for example \"2 Positions\" \u2014 so the labels do not overlap. Click the badge to expand the group and work with each level individually.</p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#setting-or-moving-a-stop-or-a-take-profit","title":"Setting or moving a stop or a take-profit","text":"<ol> <li>Click the position's or order's label on the chart to edit it.</li> <li>Drag the SL or TP line to a new price. If there is no stop or take-profit yet, drag the +SL or +TP handle to add one. As you drag, the label shows what the profit or loss would be at that price, so you can judge the level before you commit.</li> <li>To remove a stop or take-profit, click the X on its SL or TP label.</li> <li>Click the tick to send the changes to your broker, or the cross to undo them. If you move both the stop and the take-profit, one tick saves both.</li> </ol> <p>Dragging a pending order's own line, then clicking the tick, changes the price at which it will trigger.</p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#changing-a-pending-orders-amount","title":"Changing a pending order's amount","text":"<ol> <li>Click the pencil on the order's label.</li> <li>Click the amount at the left of the label and use + or \u2212 to change it. It stays within the instrument's minimum, maximum and step.</li> <li>Click the tick. The order is changed on the server, exactly as with Modify Order. If you also dragged the line, the new price is sent at the same time.</li> </ol> <p>Open positions have no amount box; to reduce a position, close part of it (6.4.3).</p> Watch how: Change an order's amount on the chart (0:42) <p></p> Watch how: Move stop loss / take profit on the chart (0:41) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#closing-from-the-chart","title":"Closing from the chart","text":"<p>Each position line has an X on its label. Clicking it opens the Close Position window, so nothing closes until you confirm. You can close all of the position, or just part of it by changing the amount, then click Ok.</p> <p>The X on a pending order's line asks you to confirm before the order is removed.</p> Watch how: Close a trade from the chart (0:35) <p></p> <p>Quick Trade closes at once</p> <p>If Quick Trade is switched on, the X closes the position, or removes the order, straight away without asking.</p>"},{"location":"charts/trading-from-chart.html#placing-an-order-from-the-chart","title":"Placing an order from the chart","text":"<ol> <li>Point at the price you want on the chart. A + button appears on the right (\"Place order at this price\"). Click it.</li> <li>Choose the order from the short menu. It offers a Sell order and a Buy order at that price \u2014 below the market, for example, Buy Limit or Sell Stop.</li> <li>A draft order line appears at that price. Nothing is sent yet. You can change its size, and drag SL and TP to add a stop-loss and a take-profit \u2014 the label shows what you would lose or gain at each level.</li> <li>Click the tick to place the order, or the cross to abandon it. The order then appears on the chart and in the Pending tab.</li> </ol> <p>A draft Buy Limit line with its SL and TP handles, the projected loss and profit on their labels, and the tick and cross buttons.</p> Watch how: Place an order from the chart (0:51) <p></p> <p>The Trade from Charts button on the chart toolbar, to the right of the gear, turns these chart-trading tools on and off. While it is off, your position and order lines are hidden.</p> <p>For an order at the current market price, the Buy/Sell strip above the chart is quicker \u2014 see The Chart. One click on Buy or Sell there places the order straight away, so check the size first.</p> Watch how: One-click Buy/Sell above the chart (0:28) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html","title":"What the Chart Shows","text":""},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#what-the-chart-shows","title":"What the Chart Shows","text":""},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#instrument","title":"Instrument","text":"<p>Click an instrument in the watchlist to load it, or select it and press Enter. Moving through the watchlist with the arrow keys does not change the chart until you click or press Enter.</p> <p>With Linked switched on, every chart follows your selection; with it off, only the active chart changes \u2014 the one you last clicked.</p> <p>You can also pick an instrument from the chart itself: click the instrument name at the top left of the chart to open Select Symbol, type part of the name in the search box, and click the one you want.</p> Watch how: Show several charts at once (1:08) <p></p> <p>Open a chart by typing</p> <p>Press Ctrl+K to open the command palette, type chart followed by the instrument, for example chart EURUSD, and press Enter.</p> Watch how: Command palette, Help and sounds (1:07) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#timeframe","title":"Timeframe","text":"<p>The timeframe button on the chart toolbar sets how much time each candle covers. Ten timeframes are available, in two groups:</p> <p>Intraday: 1m \u00b7 5m \u00b7 15m \u00b7 30m \u00b7 1h \u00b7 4h \u00b7 8h</p> <p>Daily +: 1D \u00b7 1W \u00b7 1M</p> <p>A new chart opens on 1-minute candles showing the last day.</p> Watch how: Read the chart (0:52) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#date-range","title":"Date range","text":"<p>The buttons along the bottom of the chart set how far back the view reaches. The timeframe adjusts automatically so the range stays readable:</p> <p>1D \u00b7 5D \u00b7 1M \u00b7 3M \u00b7 6M \u00b7 1Y \u00b7 5Y \u00b7 All</p> <p>You can also scroll back through history by dragging the chart sideways, and zoom with the mouse wheel. Older candles load as you scroll.</p> <p>If you do not need these buttons, you can hide them: open Panels on the right-hand strip and switch off Chart bottom bar.</p> Watch how: Chart date range and style (0:57) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#go-to-a-date","title":"Go to a date","text":"<p>The calendar button at the bottom left of the chart jumps the chart to a day. Type the date (month first), then click Go. If that day is older than the candles already loaded, the chart loads more history until it gets there. The day starts at midnight in the time zone you chose in Settings. If the date falls on a weekend or holiday, the chart goes to the nearest trading day before it. If the date is too far back for the timeframe, a short message says so; pick a larger timeframe and try again.</p> <p> </p> <p>The calendar button at the bottom left of the chart with the date box and the Go button.</p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#price-scale","title":"Price scale","text":"<p>The three buttons next to the calendar change the price scale on the right:</p> Button What it does % Shows prices as a percentage change instead of the price itself. log Uses a logarithmic scale, which is easier to read over long periods. auto Fits the scale to the candles on screen as you scroll. It is on by default. Watch how: Go to a date and price scale (0:43) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#chart-style","title":"Chart style","text":"<p>The chart-type button on the toolbar changes how prices are drawn. The names below are the ones shown in the list.</p> Style Best for Candles The default. Each candle shows open, high, low and close. Hollow Candles with unfilled bodies on rising periods. OHLC Open-high-low-close bars, a more compact alternative to candles. Line A single line through closing prices \u2014 useful for seeing the overall trend. Area A line with the area beneath it shaded. Heikin Ashi Averaged candles that smooth out noise and make trends easier to read. Volume Candles Candles whose width reflects how much was traded. Line with Markers A closing-price line with a dot at each candle. Step Line A line that moves in steps from one close to the next. HLC Area Shades the range between the high and the low, with the close marked. Baseline Shades above and below a reference level, so gains and losses stand out. Columns A column for each closing price. High-low A simple bar from each candle's high to its low. Watch how: Chart date range and style (0:57) <p></p>"},{"location":"charts/what-the-chart-shows.html#bar-replay","title":"Bar Replay","text":"<p>Bar Replay plays the market back candle by candle, so you can practise or check an idea without waiting for new prices.</p> <ol> <li>Click Replay on the chart toolbar. A replay bar opens under the chart.</li> <li>Click the candle where the replay should start. Everything after it is hidden. The arrow next to Select bar can instead start from a date, from the first candle, or from a random candle.</li> <li>Click Play to add the next candles one by one, and click it again to pause. The step button moves forward one candle at a time.</li> <li>Use the speed button (from 0.1x to 10x) to play faster or slower.</li> <li>Click the X at the right of the replay bar to end the replay and return to the live chart.</li> </ol> <p>Nothing you do in a replay sends an order, and the live chart is not changed.</p> <p> </p> <p>The chart cut off at the chosen candle, with the replay bar underneath: Select bar, Play, Step, the speed and timeframe buttons, and the X that ends the replay.</p> Watch how: Bar Replay (0:55) <p></p>"},{"location":"instruments/index.html","title":"The Instruments Tab","text":""},{"location":"instruments/index.html#the-instruments-tab","title":"The Instruments Tab","text":"<p>This tab is the full catalogue of every instrument your broker offers. Use it for research: it shows more detail per instrument than the watchlist, and it has a detail panel with contract specifications, pivot points and related news.</p> <p> </p> <p>The search bar, the instruments grouped by type, and the detail panel for the selected instrument on the right.</p> Watch how: Browse all instruments (1:45) <p></p>"},{"location":"instruments/index.html#in-this-section","title":"In this section","text":"Page Finding an Instrument Search and the grouped list Instruments Columns What each column shows The Detail Panel Prices, range, contract details and news for one instrument Pivot Points Five pivot formulas Adding to a Watchlist Put an instrument on your own watchlist The Right-Click Menu Chart, alert and order actions The News Panel Market news beside the list"},{"location":"instruments/add-to-watchlist.html","title":"Adding to a Watchlist","text":""},{"location":"instruments/add-to-watchlist.html#adding-to-a-watchlist","title":"Adding to a Watchlist","text":"<p>The Add to Watchlist button in the detail panel adapts to how many watchlists you have:</p> <ul> <li>None \u2014 creates one called \"My Watchlist\" and adds the instrument.</li> <li>One \u2014 adds or removes the instrument directly. The button reads \"Add to  Watchlist\", or \"Added to  Watchlist\" once it is in.</li> <li>Two or more \u2014 opens a list where you tick the ones you want, then press Done.</li> </ul> <p>The star fills in when the instrument is in at least one of your lists. Back on the Trading tab, the instrument now appears in that watchlist.</p> Watch how: Add to a watchlist from Instruments, and news (1:00) <p></p>"},{"location":"instruments/columns.html","title":"Instruments Columns","text":""},{"location":"instruments/columns.html#instruments-columns","title":"Instruments Columns","text":"<p>Fifteen columns are available; seven are hidden by default. Right-click a header and choose Customize\u2026 to show, hide or reorder them, or \"Set width to fit data\" to size a column to its contents. Drag the edge of a header to make a column wider or narrower.</p> Watch how: Choose and resize table columns (0:40) <p></p> Column Shows Default Instrument Symbol and name. Shown Bid The price you sell at. Shown Ask The price you buy at. Shown % Change Percentage change since the session opened. Shown High Today's highest Bid. Shown Low Today's lowest Ask. Shown NetChg Change since the session opened, in pips. Shown Time When this instrument last changed price. Shown Pip Value What one pip is worth per lot. Hidden MaxVol The largest size your broker will accept, shown in the size unit you chose in Settings (lots or amount). Blank if your broker sets no limit. Hidden Roll. Sell Rollover charged or paid on a Sell held overnight, as your broker sends it. Green is a credit, red is a charge. Hidden Roll. Buy The same for a Buy. Hidden ImmD Minimum distance in pips for immediate execution. Hidden Trade Step The smallest size increment your broker allows, in lots. Hidden NT Interval A daily no-trade break window, in the server's time. Shows a dash if the instrument has none. Hidden"},{"location":"instruments/detail-panel.html","title":"The Detail Panel","text":""},{"location":"instruments/detail-panel.html#the-detail-panel","title":"The Detail Panel","text":"<p>Click any row to slide out a detail panel on the right. The first time you open the tab, the panel already shows a common instrument, so you can see what it offers straight away. Press Escape or the \u00d7 to close it. It shows, top to bottom:</p> <p> </p> <p>Live prices, the day\u2019s range, contract specifications, pivot points and related news for the selected instrument.</p> Watch how: See an instrument's details and pivots (0:50) <p></p> <ul> <li>The symbol and full instrument name.</li> <li>SELL and BUY price cards, which update live and flash as the price moves.</li> <li>Spread in pips, with the raw price difference in brackets, and the day's change in pips and percent.</li> <li>Today's Range \u2014 a bar showing where the current price sits between the day's low and high. It updates as new highs and lows are made.</li> <li>Roll Sell and Roll Buy \u2014 overnight interest rates.</li> <li>Contract Info \u2014 Min Lot, Max Lot, Step (in lots), Max Volume, Pip Value and any no-trade Break window.</li> <li>Pivot points \u2014 see 7.4.</li> <li>Sell, Chart and Buy buttons.</li> <li>An Add to Watchlist button with a star \u2014 see 7.5.</li> <li>Related News \u2014 headlines matching this instrument's currencies or symbol. Right-click a headline for Copy Headline or Open in Browser. If nothing matches, it reads \"No recent news\".</li> </ul>"},{"location":"instruments/finding.html","title":"Finding an Instrument","text":""},{"location":"instruments/finding.html#finding-an-instrument","title":"Finding an Instrument","text":"<p>The search box at the top filters by symbol or by name, across every category at once. Matching text is highlighted. Press Escape to clear it, or the Down arrow to move into the list. Alt+F also jumps to the search box.</p> <p>With the box empty, instruments are grouped by asset class \u2014 Forex, Crypto, Indices, Commodities, Stocks, ETF and Other. Each group shows its first ten instruments with a count badge. Click a group header to collapse or expand it, and use \"Show more\" at the foot of a group to load another fifty. \"\u2190 Show Less\" returns to ten. A sticky header keeps the current group's name visible while you scroll.</p> Watch how: See an instrument's details and pivots (0:50) <p></p> <p>While the list is loading it reads \"Loading instruments\u2026\"; if nothing matches, \"No instruments found\". The status bar beneath shows the total count (for example \"640 instruments\") and the time of the last price update (for example \"Updated 14:32:05\").</p>"},{"location":"instruments/news.html","title":"The News Panel","text":""},{"location":"instruments/news.html#the-news-panel","title":"The News Panel","text":"<p>The panel on the far right, headed Market News, shows the latest stories as they come in. Its header has a coloured dot \u2014 green when the feed is connected, pulsing when it is not \u2014 and a badge counting headlines that arrived while you were looking elsewhere. Click a headline to open it in your browser; right-click for Copy headline, Copy link and Open in browser.</p> Watch how: Add to a watchlist from Instruments, and news (1:00) <p></p> <p>When there is no news it reads \"Waiting for news\u2026\", or \"Connecting to news feed\u2026\" followed by \"Check Settings \u2192 News Feeds\" if it cannot connect. Toggle the panel with Alt+W while on this tab, or from the Panels icon on the right strip. Drag its left edge to resize it between 180 and 480 pixels.</p>"},{"location":"instruments/pivot-points.html","title":"Pivot Points","text":""},{"location":"instruments/pivot-points.html#pivot-points","title":"Pivot Points","text":"<p>The pivot strip shows support and resistance levels worked out from the previous day's prices, with a marker showing where the price is now. Click the method name (for example \"Camarilla Pivots \u25be\") to choose a different formula:</p> <p> </p> <p>Nine levels from S4 to R4 with the current price marked. Click the method name to change formula.</p> Watch how: See an instrument's details and pivots (0:50) <p></p> Watch how: More from the Instruments tab (0:35) <p></p> Method Levels Notes Classic S4 to R4 (nine levels) The standard calculation from the previous day's high, low and close. Woodie S4 to R4 Weights today's opening price more heavily. Needs today's open, so it waits until the session starts. Camarilla S4 to R4 Wider levels intended for range trading. This is the default. Fibonacci S4 to R4 Levels spaced by Fibonacci ratios. DeMark S1, P, R1 (three levels) Defines only one level either side; the strip is shorter as a result. <p>Your choice is remembered and applies to every instrument. Hovering a band shows the two levels and the price range between them.</p> <p>The strip shows \"Loading pivots\u2026\" while it fetches data, \"Pivot points \u2014 no previous day data\" after a weekend or holiday, and \"Waiting for today's opening price\u2026\" for Woodie and DeMark before the session opens.</p>"},{"location":"instruments/right-click-menu.html","title":"The Right-Click Menu","text":""},{"location":"instruments/right-click-menu.html#the-right-click-menu","title":"The Right-Click Menu","text":"<p>Right-click an instrument (or press the Menu key) for: Open Chart (Alt+N), Price Alert (Alt+P), Market Order Buy (Alt+B), Market Order Sell (Alt+S), the four Entry order types (Entry Stop Buy, Entry Limit Buy, Entry Stop Sell, Entry Limit Sell), the two OCO types (Entry OCO Buy, Entry OCO Sell), Find Instrument (Alt+F), Filters (it reads Hide Filters while they are showing), and Clear All Filters.</p> <p>It is the same set as the watchlist, minus the watchlist-specific items such as Add to Watchlist. To add an instrument to a watchlist from this tab, use the detail panel (see 7.5).</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/index.html","title":"The Strategy Marketplace","text":""},{"location":"marketplace/index.html#the-strategy-marketplace","title":"The Strategy Marketplace","text":"<p>The Marketplace tab is where you find ready-made ActFX strategies, and where you share your own. It is the last tab, after Analytics.</p> <p> </p> <p>Strategy cards with their author, price and category. The chips at the top filter by favourites, purchases and category.</p> Watch how: Browse the Marketplace (1:18) <p></p> <p>The toolbar has two views:</p> View What it shows Browse Every strategy in the Marketplace, as cards. My Listings The strategies you have published (see Publishing Your Strategies). <p>Next to them are a search box and filter chips:</p> Chip What it shows All Everything. \u2605 Favourites The strategies you starred. \u2713 Purchased Strategies you bought, rented or are trying. Shown once you have one. Breakout, Mean reversion, Momentum, Trend following Strategies in that category. Only categories that have strategies are shown. <p>The count on the right says how many strategies match.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/index.html#strategy-cards","title":"Strategy cards","text":"<p>Each card shows the name, the author, a short summary, the price and the category.</p> <ul> <li>by ActTrader \u2713: a strategy supplied by ActTrader. These are the fourteen strategies that used to be built into ActFX.</li> <li>by another name: a strategy another trader published. Click the name to see only that author's strategies. A chip with the author's name appears in the toolbar; click its \u00d7 to show everyone again.</li> <li>Free or a price such as 10.00 USD/mo: what it costs (see Paid Strategies).</li> <li>Added: you already have a copy in ActFX.</li> <li>\u2605 and the copy count: how many traders starred it and how many added it.</li> </ul> <p> </p> <p>The description, the symbols it suits, its inputs, and the Add to My Strategies button.</p> <p>Click a card to open its details on the right: description, screenshots, the symbols and timeframe it suits, and its inputs with their default values. Click \u00d7 at the top of the details to close them.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/index.html#in-this-section","title":"In this section","text":"Page Adding Strategies Add a free strategy to ActFX, star favourites, make copies Publishing Your Strategies Share a strategy, update it, take it down Paid Strategies Test, try, rent or buy a paid strategy Reporting a Strategy Tell ActTrader about a harmful or misleading strategy"},{"location":"marketplace/adding.html","title":"Adding Strategies","text":""},{"location":"marketplace/adding.html#adding-strategies","title":"Adding Strategies","text":"<p>To use a free strategy, add it to My Strategies in ActFX.</p> Watch how: Add a strategy to ActFX (0:55) <p></p> <ol> <li>Open the Marketplace tab and click a strategy with a Free badge.</li> <li>In the details, click Add to My Strategies.</li> <li>A message confirms it. The button changes to \u2713 In My Strategies and the card shows Added.</li> </ol> <p>The copy appears in ActFX \u2192 Strategies, under My Strategies. It is yours: you can run it, test it, change it in the Editor, rename it or delete it. Each strategy is added once; adding it again does not make a second copy.</p> <p>If you have no strategies yet, ActFX shows a link, \"or add a ready-made strategy from the Marketplace\", that opens the Marketplace tab.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/adding.html#favourites","title":"Favourites","text":"<p>Click the \u2606 on a card, or in the details, to star a strategy. Starring does not add it. Use the \u2605 Favourites chip to see your starred strategies. Click the star again to remove it.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/adding.html#making-a-copy","title":"Making a copy","text":"<p>To keep a second version to experiment with, right-click a strategy in ActFX and choose Make a Copy. The copy is added to My Strategies with \"Copy\" at the end of its name.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/adding.html#your-strategies-on-other-computers","title":"Your strategies on other computers","text":"<p>Your strategies are saved to your account, so the same list appears when you log in on another computer. They are saved when you log in and shortly after each change. Click \u21bb Refresh on the ActFX toolbar to save and fetch them straight away.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html","title":"Paid Strategies","text":""},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html#paid-strategies","title":"Paid Strategies","text":"<p>Some strategies cost money. A paid card shows its price, for example 10.00 USD/mo for a rent, or 89.99 USD \u00b7 29.99 USD/mo when you can buy or rent it.</p> Watch how: Try a paid strategy (1:04) <p></p> <p>Open a paid strategy to see its price and any free trial, for example \"Price: 10.00 USD / month (1-day free trial)\".</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html#test-it-first","title":"Test it first","text":"<p>Click Test it - no purchase needed. The strategy opens in ActFX \u2192 Tester with its inputs ready. Pick symbols and press Start to back-test it on past prices. You cannot run it on your account until you have a licence.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html#try-it-free","title":"Try it free","text":"<p>If the seller offers a trial, click Try free for the number of days shown. Trials are for demo accounts only, once per strategy. The trial starts at once. The details then show when it ends and that the strategy is in ActFX \u2192 Strategies, under Purchased.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html#rent-or-buy","title":"Rent or buy","text":"<p>Click Rent or Buy. This sends a request to your broker, and the details show \"Request sent\". Pay your broker as they tell you. The strategy is yours as soon as they confirm. If they decline, the details show their reason.</p> <p>Your broker may ask for your user ID. It is shown under the buttons; click Copy to copy it.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/paid.html#using-a-purchased-strategy","title":"Using a purchased strategy","text":"<p>A strategy you bought, rented or are trying shows \u2713 Owned on its card. It is listed under the \u2713 Purchased chip in the Marketplace, and in ActFX \u2192 Strategies under Purchased; Show in ActFX in its details takes you there. You can run and test it, but its code is not shown, so the right-click menu offers only Run and Test.</p> Watch how: Use a purchased strategy (0:52) <p></p> <p>The details show what you have: \"Bought - it never ends\", or the plan and the date it ends. The app checks your licence while a purchased strategy runs. Three days before a rent or trial ends you get a reminder. When it ends, the strategy stops; rent it again to keep using it.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/publishing.html","title":"Publishing Your Strategies","text":""},{"location":"marketplace/publishing.html#publishing-your-strategies","title":"Publishing Your Strategies","text":"<p>You can share any strategy in My Strategies with other traders. It goes live in the Marketplace as soon as you publish it.</p> Watch how: Publish your strategy (1:23) <p></p>"},{"location":"marketplace/publishing.html#publishing-a-strategy","title":"Publishing a strategy","text":"<ol> <li>In ActFX \u2192 Strategies, right-click the strategy and choose Publish to Marketplace\u2026.</li> <li> <p>Fill in the form:</p> Field Your name as the author Shown on all your strategies. You enter it the first time and can change it here later. Summary One or two sentences, shown on the card. Up to 300 characters. Required. How it works A longer description for the details. Optional. Category Trend following, Mean reversion, Breakout, Momentum, Scalping, Grid, Multi symbol or Other. Timeframe The timeframe it is meant for, or Any timeframe. Symbols The symbols it suits, for example EURUSD, GBPUSD. Tags Words that help traders find it, separated by commas. Screenshots Up to 5 images (PNG, JPEG or WebP, 2 MB each). Price Free, Rent, Buy, or Rent or buy. </li> <li> <p>Click Publish. The app checks the strategy first: it must compile, and it is run briefly on past prices to make sure it does not stop with an error. A message confirms when it is live.</p> </li> </ol> <p> </p> <p>Author name, summary, description, category, timeframe, symbols, tags, screenshots and price.</p> <p>The strategy's inputs are listed in the Marketplace from its code, with their default values.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/publishing.html#price","title":"Price","text":"Price What traders get Free Anyone can add it to My Strategies and see and change the code. Rent Traders pay a monthly price. You can offer a free trial of up to 30 days. Buy Traders pay once and keep it. Rent or buy Traders choose. <p>Traders who rent or buy a paid strategy can run and test it, but never see its code. Payment goes through the trader's broker (see Paid Strategies).</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/publishing.html#my-listings","title":"My Listings","text":"<p>Open the Marketplace tab and click My Listings to see everything you published, with its state:</p> State Meaning Live Traders can find it. Unpublished You took it down. Taken down ActTrader took it down after a report. The reason is shown. Taken down \u00b7 fix in review You sent a fix and ActTrader is checking it. In review ActTrader is checking it before it goes live. Changes needed ActTrader asked for changes. Their reason is shown. <p> </p> <p>Each strategy you published with its state, version, price, stars and copies.</p> <p>Each row shows the version, the price, the stars and the number of copies.</p> <ul> <li>Publish update\u2026 sends a new version after you change the strategy in ActFX. It opens the same form, filled in.</li> <li>Unpublish takes it out of the Marketplace. Copies traders already made, and licences they bought, stay with them. You can publish it again at any time.</li> <li>Publish again\u2026 puts an unpublished strategy back in the Marketplace.</li> <li>Withdraw cancels a strategy that is still in review.</li> <li>Fix and send for review appears on a strategy ActTrader took down. Change the strategy, then send it; it goes live again once ActTrader approves it.</li> </ul> <p>If you delete the strategy from ActFX, its listing stays, but it can no longer be updated.</p>"},{"location":"marketplace/reporting.html","title":"Reporting a Strategy","text":""},{"location":"marketplace/reporting.html#reporting-a-strategy","title":"Reporting a Strategy","text":"<p>If a strategy looks harmful, misleading or copied from someone else, report it to ActTrader.</p> Watch how: Report a strategy (0:43) <p></p> <ol> <li>Open the strategy in the Marketplace.</li> <li>Scroll to the bottom of the details and click Report\u2026.</li> <li>Choose a reason: Harmful or malicious code, Misleading results or claims, Copied from someone else, Spam, or Something else.</li> <li>Add details if they help. They are required for Something else.</li> <li>Click Report.</li> </ol> <p>ActTrader reads every report and decides what happens. The seller does not see who reported it. The details then show \"\u2713 You reported this strategy\".</p> <p>While the report is still open you can take it back: click Undo report.</p> <p>You cannot report your own strategies.</p>"},{"location":"messages/index.html","title":"Messages and Warnings","text":""},{"location":"messages/index.html#messages-and-warnings","title":"Messages and Warnings","text":"<p>Most messages appear as small panels in the top-right corner. They disappear on their own \u2014 after about four seconds, or six for errors \u2014 and you can dismiss one early with its \u00d7 button. A coloured bar down the left edge shows the kind of message: your broker's accent colour (orange by default) for information, green for success, amber for a warning, red for an error.</p> <p>Margin calls are different. When your own account gets a margin call, a red window appears in the middle of the screen and stays there until you press Dismiss (or View Position, which also takes you to the Trading tab). Clicking outside the window does not close it. If more than one is waiting, the window shows \"+1 more\" and the next one appears when you dismiss the first.</p> <p>Ordinary messages still disappear by themselves</p> <p>Order rejections, feed problems and equity warnings appear as messages that fade after a few seconds. If you step away from the screen you can miss one. Trading messages are also written to Events and Messages on the Summary tab \u2014 check there when you return.</p> <p>Turning notifications off</p> <p>Settings \u2192 Trading has a Show notifications switch. When it is off, the small messages and the event sounds are not shown, and the gear icon on the right-hand strip carries a small dot to remind you. Margin-call windows are always shown, and Events and Messages keeps recording everything.</p>"},{"location":"messages/index.html#message-lists","title":"Message lists","text":"Page Margin and Equity Warnings Margin calls and equity warnings Order and Trade Messages Orders placed, filled, rejected Connection Messages Lost and restored connections Price Alert Messages When an alert is reached Chart Trading Messages Trading from the chart Login Errors Problems logging in <p>The complete list of every message is in Appendix A.</p>"},{"location":"messages/chart-trading.html","title":"Chart Trading Messages","text":""},{"location":"messages/chart-trading.html#chart-trading-messages","title":"Chart Trading Messages","text":"Message Meaning No instrument selected \u2014 select a symbol first The chart has no instrument loaded. No live price for EURUSD No price has arrived for this instrument yet. Invalid lot size The size in the Buy/Sell strip above the chart is zero or not usable. Chart produced an invalid price value \u2014 drag cancelled The dragged level was not usable. Try again. Order #161203 may have been filled or cancelled The order you dragged no longer exists. Check the Pending tab. Position #98765 may have already been closed The position you dragged is gone. This chart action isn't recognized \u2014 please use the position/order panel instead The chart sent an action the application does not handle. Use the Open or Pending tab instead. <p>Adding, moving or removing a stop or limit on the chart uses the same request as the Stop and Limit dialogs. If your broker refuses it, you see \"Order failed\" with your broker's reason beneath.</p> <p>Clicking the \u00d7 on a position or order line on the chart asks first: it opens the Close Position window, or asks you to confirm removing the order. With Quick Trade switched on it acts at once.</p> Watch how: Close a trade from the chart (0:35) <p></p>"},{"location":"messages/connection.html","title":"Connection Messages","text":""},{"location":"messages/connection.html#connection-messages","title":"Connection Messages","text":"Message Kind Meaning and what to do Connected \u2014 live prices Success Reconnected after an interruption. Nothing to do. Offline mode \u2014 simulated prices Warning Your session with the broker was lost and the application could not log you back in yet. It keeps trying by itself. Prices are not live \u2014 do not trade until the connection indicator turns green again. No Feed: Buy EURUSD 1 lots queued \u2014 will submit when feed restores Warning You placed an order while the price feed was down. It is held, not sent. Feed restored \u2014 3 queued order(s) submitted as pending Success Held orders have now been sent as pending orders. Check the Pending tab. <p>A dropped price feed on its own does not show a message \u2014 watch the connection indicator. It reads \"No Prices \u2014 retrying\u2026\" while prices are stalled and \"Offline \u2014 reconnecting\u2026\" while the session is lost. If orders are being held it says so, for example \"No Prices \u2014 2 order(s) queued\". See Connection Status.</p> <p>Orders placed while disconnected become pending orders</p> <p>An order you place during a feed outage is held, and when the connection returns it is submitted as a pending order at the price recorded at the time \u2014 not as a market order at the current price. Check the Pending tab after any outage.</p>"},{"location":"messages/login.html","title":"Login Errors","text":""},{"location":"messages/login.html#login-errors","title":"Login Errors","text":"Message Meaning and what to do Wrong Account Type or Username or Password Your credentials were not accepted. Check the server, account and password, minding capitals. This broker's server rejected the login due to a server-side error. Please contact your broker's support \u2014 this is not a credentials problem. A fault on your broker's server. Your details are fine. Contact your broker. Login failed \u2014 the server returned an unexpected response. Please try again or contact support. The reply could not be understood. Try again; if it persists, contact support. <p>Other messages come straight from your broker's server and are shown as received \u2014 for example, a message saying your user is inactive. Contact your broker about these.</p>"},{"location":"messages/margin.html","title":"Margin and Equity Warnings","text":""},{"location":"messages/margin.html#margin-and-equity-warnings","title":"Margin and Equity Warnings","text":"<p>These are the most serious messages. All are recorded in Events and Messages.</p> <p>Margin calls on your account open the red margin-call window described above, which stays on screen until you dismiss it. The text starts with \"Margin Call for Account 287\" (or \"Short Margin for Account 287\"), followed by one of the messages below. Equity warnings are ordinary amber messages that fade by themselves.</p> Message What it means What to do Margin Call Level 1! You have to make additional deposit or close one or more of your open positions\u2026 Your equity has fallen below your used margin. Positions will be hedged automatically within 24 hours if you do nothing. Deposit funds or close positions to bring equity back above used margin. Margin Call Overdue! All positions will be hedged within 30 minutes! The warning period has expired. Act immediately \u2014 deposit or close positions. MC Levels: Hedge All \u2014 All open positions are fully hedged. Your positions have been hedged automatically. You cannot trade further until this is resolved. Deposit funds, or close one or more hedged pairs. MC Levels: Close All \u2014 All open postions are closed! The most severe outcome. Every position has been closed by your broker. Review your closed positions and account balance before trading again. Margin Call! Some positions will be closed! Your broker is about to close some of your positions. Act immediately \u2014 deposit or close positions. Margin Call released! Resume trading! Your account has recovered and normal trading is available. Nothing. Short Margin! You have to make additional deposit or close one or more of your open positions\u2026 Your balance has fallen below your used margin. Some positions will be closed at end of day if you do nothing. Deposit funds or reduce your exposure before the trading day ends. Short Margin Overdue! Some positions will be closed! The short-margin period has expired. Act immediately. Margin Call on account #287. The following open positions are closed: \u2026 Your broker has closed positions. The list of closed tickets follows. Review your closed positions and balance. Account 287. Equity has reached 45% of Used Margin. An early warning that your equity is being consumed. Shown as a fading amber message. Review your open positions and consider reducing size. Account 287. Equity has reached the minimum. Your equity is at the account minimum. Shown as a fading amber message. Deposit funds or close positions. <p>A spelling error in one margin-call message</p> <p>The most severe margin-call message reads \"All open postions are closed!\" \u2014 \"postions\" instead of \"positions\". This wording is carried over from the previous Windows application. The message is genuine and means every position has been closed.</p>"},{"location":"messages/orders.html","title":"Order and Trade Messages","text":""},{"location":"messages/orders.html#order-and-trade-messages","title":"Order and Trade Messages","text":"Message Kind Meaning Buy 1.00 EURUSD @ 1.08432 Success An order from the Buy/Sell strip above the chart, or from Living Market, was accepted at that price. Order placed \u2014 #161203 Success Accepted, with the broker's order reference. Order failed Error Rejected. The reason \u2014 from your broker, or from the application's own checks \u2014 is shown beneath. Position #98765 closed Success That position is now closed. Order cancelled Info A pending order was removed. Order Executed \u2014 Buy EURUSD Success An order was filled and is now an open position \u2014 either a market order, or a pending order whose price was reached. The size, price and trade number are shown beneath. Stop loss updated Info Your stop-loss was changed by dragging it on the chart. Take profit updated Info Your take-profit was changed by dragging it on the chart. Order rate updated Info A pending order's trigger price was changed by dragging it on the chart. Order modified Info An order, stop or limit was changed from a dialog. <p>With Quick Trade switched on, an order placed by clicking a Bid or Ask cell in the watchlist shows a short note inside the watchlist instead, such as \"Buy EURUSD placed\". See A.2 for the full list.</p>"},{"location":"messages/price-alerts.html","title":"Price Alert Messages","text":""},{"location":"messages/price-alerts.html#price-alert-messages","title":"Price Alert Messages","text":"<p>When an alert triggers you see, for example: \"Price Alert: The EURUSD Bid rate has reached 1.08500\".</p> <p>Price alerts are kept on your broker's server, not on your computer. They stay in place when you close the application, and your broker's server decides when they fire.</p> <p>An alert fires once and is then removed</p> <p>When an alert fires it is taken off your Price Alerts list. Set it up again if you want to be warned a second time.</p> <p>Alert prices are always shown to five decimal places, so an alert on a Japanese yen pair at 151.25 is displayed as 151.25000.</p> Message Kind Meaning Price alerts are unavailable: the broker's alert server could not be reached. Warning Your alerts could not be loaded. Add Alert stays greyed out until they can be. The price alert could not be saved. Error Your broker did not accept the alert. If your broker gave a reason, it is added after a colon. Price alerts are not available right now. Error You tried to add or change an alert while the alert service was not available. Unknown instrument EURUSD Error The instrument could not be matched to one your broker offers."},{"location":"more/index.html","title":"Reports, Living Market and Analytics","text":""},{"location":"more/index.html#reports-living-market-and-analytics","title":"Reports, Living Market and Analytics","text":"Page Reports Your account statement and other broker reports Living Market A live map of currency strength, and picking a trade from it Analytics Your trading performance: figures, calendar, charts and AI Health Score <p>For automated trading, see ActFX Strategies.</p> <p>Guided tours</p> <p>The ActFX, Living Market and Analytics tabs each have a short guided tour. Click the ? at the right end of the tab row (\"Take a tour of this workspace\") to start it.</p>"},{"location":"more/analytics.html","title":"Analytics","text":""},{"location":"more/analytics.html#analytics","title":"Analytics","text":"<p>Performance dashboards built from your trading history. Eight period buttons across the top select the range \u2014 1D, 3D, 7D, 1M, 3M, 6M, 1Y and ALL \u2014 with 1M selected by default. The \u21bb button refreshes, as does F5.</p> <p> </p> <p>The six top figures, the trading calendar with the AI Health Score beside it, and the equity curve and drawdown charts below.</p> Watch how: Analytics overview (1:06) <p></p> Watch how: Analytics in depth (1:07) <p></p>"},{"location":"more/analytics.html#headline-figures","title":"Headline figures","text":"<p>Six across the top: Total PnL, Win Rate, Trades, Profit Factor, Max Drawdown and Sharpe Ratio. Four more at the bottom: Gross Profit, Gross Loss, Avg Win and Avg Loss. A dash means your broker did not supply that figure.</p>"},{"location":"more/analytics.html#trading-calendar","title":"Trading Calendar","text":"<p>A month grid with each day tinted green for profit and red for loss, showing that day's result. Four chips summarise the month: Profit Days, Loss Days, Realised PnL and End Balance. Use \u2039 and \u203a to change month, or Today to return.</p> <p>Click a day to open a detail panel beneath, with a Realised PnL Summary of ten figures, an Intraday Equity chart, and Risk &amp; Balance chips. A day with no trading reads \"No trading activity on this date\".</p>"},{"location":"more/analytics.html#charts","title":"Charts","text":"Card Contents Equity Curve Up to six series you can switch on and off: Equity (on by default), Balance, PnL, Realised, Unrealised and Lots. Lots appears only when your broker supplies lot figures. Drawdown Balance against drawdown over the period. Monthly PnL One bar per calendar month. Performance A win-rate ring with Winners and Losers, a Buy versus Sell breakdown, and Lots and Avg Hold. Instruments by Pair A ring of your most-traded instruments with total trades in the centre, and the top eight listed. Daily PnL One bar per day, with the number of profitable and losing days and the total in the card title. Holding Period How your profit and loss splits across holding times, from under a minute to over four hours. Closed PnL Overall Realised and Today's PnL. Transaction Summary Deposits, withdrawals and other account transactions."},{"location":"more/analytics.html#ai-health-score","title":"AI Health Score","text":"<p>A score out of 100 with a gauge, a risk level and a trend, plus written insights under headings such as Warning, Opportunity, Tip, Risk, Performance, Behavior and Streak. Headings with nothing to report are left out. Where a score is unavailable the card reads \"Health score is not available for this account yet.\"</p> <p>Analytics is not available for every account</p> <p>Some managed or master accounts are not registered for the analytics service. On those accounts the tab shows \"Could not load analytics\" with a Retry button instead of charts. This is an account registration matter \u2014 speak to your broker.</p>"},{"location":"more/living-market.html","title":"Living Market","text":""},{"location":"more/living-market.html#living-market","title":"Living Market","text":"<p>A visual map of currency strength. Nine currencies \u2014 USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, CHF, AUD, CAD, NZD and HKD \u2014 are shown as circles, sized and coloured by how strong each one is, joined by lines representing the pairs between them. Under each circle a small figure shows how much that currency has moved, in green when it is getting stronger and red when it is getting weaker. Thicker, brighter lines mean the two currencies disagree more \u2014 which is where movement tends to be.</p> <p> </p> <p>Session dial (top left), narration (top right), the currency constellation (centre), and the action card (bottom).</p> Watch how: Read the Living Market map (1:40) <p></p> Area What it shows SESSION Which trading sessions are open \u2014 Sydney, Tokyo, London, New York, combinations such as \"London + New York\", or Closed. With the current day and UTC time beneath. NARRATION A plain-language sentence about the pair you have selected. Before you pick one it reads \"Pick a pair on the map. Lines run thicker where the two currencies disagree most.\" Constellation Click a currency to show only its pairs; click it again to clear. Click a line to select that pair. Hovering a currency shows its strength percentage. ACTION The selected pair (or \"Select a pair on the map\"), a CONVICTION slider that sets the trade size in lots, and SELL and BUY buttons showing the live Bid and Ask. Both are disabled until you select a pair. <p>Clicking SELL or BUY places a market order straight away for the size shown \u2014 there is no separate order ticket.</p> Watch how: Pick and size a trade in Living Market (0:36) <p></p> <p>If a correlation risk is detected \u2014 several of your open positions exposed to the same move \u2014 a red CORRELATION RISK banner appears across the top with a headline and a Dismiss button.</p>"},{"location":"more/reports.html","title":"Reports","text":""},{"location":"more/reports.html#reports","title":"Reports","text":"<p>This tab displays reports your broker hosts \u2014 account statements and similar \u2014 inside the application. It has a small toolbar with Back (\u2190), Forward (\u2192) and Reload (\u21bb) buttons, and shows the page title in the centre.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Account Statement setup page: report type, time period, which accounts to include, and print options.</p> Watch how: Get your account statement (0:56) <p></p> Watch how: Trading Statistics report (0:41) <p></p> <p>What the page contains is supplied by your broker, so it may differ from the example shown. A typical Account Statement page offers:</p> Section What you choose Report type Tabs across the top \u2014 for example Account Statement and Trading Statistics. Time Format The period to cover: Day, Week, Month, Quarter, Year, Since open, Previous month, Previous quarter, Previous year, or User defined with your own From and Till dates. The time zone in use is stated beside it. Accounts setup All Accounts or a single account, plus options such as Simple form, Show Comments, Group by instrument type and Show balance and equity, and the size format to report in. Print setup Rows per page and text size, with a recommended setting noted. Run Report Builds the report with the choices above. <p>While a report loads it shows \"Loading report\u2026\". The report itself is shown on a white page, as it would be in a web browser. If your broker does not provide reports, the tab reads \"Reports not available for this account\".</p> <p>If the broker's report page cannot build a report, its error message is shown to you as an error notice, so a failed report does not simply look as if nothing happened. Such errors come from the broker's server \u2014 if one keeps appearing, contact your broker.</p>"},{"location":"overview/index.html","title":"Overview","text":""},{"location":"overview/index.html#overview","title":"Overview","text":"<p>ActTrader is a desktop trading platform. You connect it to your broker with the account details your broker gave you, and it brings live prices, charts, order placement, position management, account reports and automated trading together in one window.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Trading tab: the tabs across the top, the watchlist on the left, the chart in the centre, your positions at the bottom and the account bar along the foot of the window.</p> Watch how: Find your way around the screen (1:24) <p></p>"},{"location":"overview/index.html#the-eight-tabs","title":"The eight tabs","text":"Tab What it is for Trading Your main screen: the watchlist, charts, and your open positions, pending orders and closed trades. Instruments Everything your broker offers, grouped by type, with a detail panel and pivot points. Summary Your accounts, positions by instrument, the events log, risk exposure and price alerts, on one screen. Reports Your broker's reports, such as the account statement. ActFX Write, test and run automated trading strategies. Living Market A live map of currency strength and how currency pairs relate. Analytics Your trading performance: profit and loss, win rate, equity curve, a trading calendar and an AI health score. Marketplace Ready-made strategies to add, try or buy, and the place to share your own. Watch how: The eight tabs (0:57)"},{"location":"overview/index.html#around-the-edges","title":"Around the edges","text":"<ul> <li>Top left: your broker's logo opens the account menu (switch or add accounts). Beside it, the connection status.</li> <li>Right-hand strip: icons for the theme, panels, news, help and settings. See The Right-Hand Icon Strip.</li> <li>Bottom bar: your Balance, Equity, Usable Margin, Used Margin and Net P/L, always visible. See The Account Status Bar.</li> </ul> <p>New to the terms used on screen? See the Glossary.</p>"},{"location":"overview/glossary.html","title":"Glossary","text":""},{"location":"overview/glossary.html#glossary","title":"Glossary","text":"<p>These are the terms used on screen in this application. Definitions describe what each term means in this product specifically.</p> Term as shown Meaning Instrument Anything you can trade \u2014 a currency pair, a stock, an index, a commodity, a crypto pair or an ETF. Bid The price at which you sell. Shown in the Bid column and on the Sell button. Always the lower of the two prices. Ask The price at which you buy. Shown in the Ask column and on the Buy button. Always the higher of the two prices. Sprd / Spread The gap between Ask and Bid, in pips. This is your immediate cost to open a position. Lot The size of a trade. How this is displayed is your choice \u2014 see Full Amount, Amount, K and Lots below. Full Amount Trade size shown as the full base-currency figure, for example 100,000. In tables the column is headed Amount. Amount, K Trade size shown in thousands, for example 100K. In tables the column is headed Amt,K. Lots Trade size shown as a multiple of the contract size, for example 0.10. This is the default. In tables the column is headed Lot. Ticket The broker's unique number for one open or closed position. The column tooltip calls it the Ticket Number. Trade ID A second reference number for a position. Its column is hidden by default; you can show it with Customize. Order An instruction that has not been filled yet. It sits in Pending Orders until its trigger price is reached. Position A filled trade that is currently open and making or losing money as the price moves. B/S Whether a position or order is a Buy or a Sell. Stop Your stop-loss price. Closes the position automatically to cap a loss. Limit Your take-profit price. Closes the position automatically to bank a profit. Tr.Stop Trailing stop distance in pips. The stop follows the price when it moves in your favour, and never moves against you. Trader Range How much price slippage you will accept when an order fills, in pips. Zero means fill at the exact price only. Proximity How far a pending order's trigger price is from the current market price, in pips. Balance Your cash, not counting the profit or loss on positions that are still open. Equity Balance plus the profit or loss on your open positions. What your account is worth right now. Used Margin The portion of your equity the broker is currently holding as collateral for your open positions. UsableMargin Equity minus Used Margin. What you have left to open new positions with. Shown as UsblMrgn in the Summary Accounts table. Margin level Used Margin as a percentage of Equity, shown on the status bar as a coloured bar with a percentage. Green below 100%, amber 100\u2013149%, red at 150% and above. Net PL The net profit or loss on your currently open positions only. It does not include trades you have already closed. Lot P/L Profit or loss expressed in points per single lot, rather than in money. Com Commission charged by your broker. Displayed as a negative number because it is a cost. Roll / Prm Rollover interest, charged or paid for holding a position overnight. Shown as Roll in the Summary Accounts table and as Prm (Premium) in the positions tables. NH / Non-Hedged The uncovered part of a hedged position \u2014 where your Buy and Sell sizes in the same instrument do not cancel out. Hedge Opening an opposite position in the same instrument instead of closing the one you hold. OCO One Cancels Other. Two orders placed together; when one fills, the other is cancelled automatically. Entry order An order that opens a position when the price reaches a level you set, rather than immediately. Quick Trade A mode that adds a lot-size box to every watchlist row. One click on a Bid or Ask price then trades at once, with no ticket and no confirmation. Watchlist Your own named list of instruments, shown as a tab under the category tabs above the instrument list. Pivot points Support and resistance levels worked out from the previous day's prices. Five formulas are offered. ActFX The scripting language and workspace used for automated strategies in this application."},{"location":"quick-start/index.html","title":"Quick Start: Your First Five Minutes","text":""},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#quick-start-your-first-five-minutes","title":"Quick Start: Your First Five Minutes","text":"<p>If you have used a trading platform before, these five steps are enough to get you trading. Each step links to the full instructions.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#1-log-in","title":"1. Log in","text":"<p>Choose your broker in Server, enter your Account ID and Password, and click Login. Tick Remember me to have them filled in next time. Full instructions</p> Watch how: Log in to ActTrader (0:51) <p></p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#2-find-an-instrument","title":"2. Find an instrument","text":"<p>The watchlist runs down the left of the Trading tab. Click a category tab (All, Forex, Crypto, Indices, Commodities, Stocks, ETF) or type in the search box to find any instrument by symbol or name. Click a row to show it on the chart. More about the watchlist</p> Watch how: Read the watchlist (1:50) <p></p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#3-place-your-first-trade","title":"3. Place your first trade","text":"<ol> <li>Click the Ask price to buy, or the Bid price to sell. The Deal Ticket opens.</li> <li>Check the Amount.</li> <li>Click Buy or Sell.</li> </ol> <p>A message confirms the order, and the position appears on the Open tab at the bottom of the screen. Full instructions</p> Watch how: Quick order and hedge (0:41) <p></p> <p>Orders are sent straight away</p> <p>Clicking Buy or Sell sends a live order immediately. Check the amount before you click.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#4-protect-and-manage-the-trade","title":"4. Protect and manage the trade","text":"<p>On the Open tab:</p> <ul> <li>Click the trade's Stop cell to set a stop loss, or its Limit cell to set a take profit.</li> <li>Click the \u2715 at the end of the row to close it. The Close Position window opens so you can confirm, or close only part.</li> </ul> <p>You can also drag the trade's stop loss and take profit on the chart. Stop Loss and Take Profit \u00b7 Close and Hedge Positions</p> Watch how: Set a stop loss and take profit (0:57) <p></p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#5-watch-your-account","title":"5. Watch your account","text":"<p>The bar along the bottom of the window always shows your Balance, Equity, Usable Margin, Used Margin and Net P/L, with a coloured bar for how much of your margin is in use. The Account Status Bar</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/index.html#where-to-go-next","title":"Where to go next","text":"If you want to\u2026 Read Understand a word on screen Glossary Arrange the screen your way Configuring Your Workspace Place other kinds of orders Trading Guide Use the chart Charts See all your accounts and positions together Summary Run an automated strategy ActFX Understand a message you have just seen Messages and Warnings Fix a problem Troubleshooting"},{"location":"quick-start/connection-states.html","title":"Connection Status","text":""},{"location":"quick-start/connection-states.html#connection-status","title":"Connection Status","text":"<p>The dot at the top left of the window tells you whether you are connected and receiving live prices. Point at its label for a longer explanation.</p> <p> </p> <p>The coloured dot and its label at the top left of the window.</p> You see What it means What to do Green dot, Connected Live prices are arriving normally. Nothing. Amber pulsing dot, No Prices \u2014 retrying\u2026 You are still logged in, but prices have stopped arriving. The last prices stay on screen and you can still trade. Wait. It recovers on its own. Red pulsing dot, Offline \u2014 reconnecting\u2026 The connection to your broker was lost. The app is reconnecting. Orders cannot be traded until it is back. Wait. It reconnects on its own. Red pulsing dot, Disconnected You are not connected. Check your internet connection. See Prices and Connection. <p>While you log in, the login screen shows progress messages such as Connecting\u2026, Logging in\u2026 and Loading instruments\u2026</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/connection-states.html#orders-placed-while-the-connection-is-down","title":"Orders placed while the connection is down","text":"<p>If you place an order while the connection is down, it is held on your computer and the status shows how many are waiting, for example No Prices \u2014 3 order(s) queued or Offline \u2014 3 order(s) queued.</p> <p>Held orders are sent as pending orders</p> <p>When the connection returns, held orders are sent as pending orders at the price you saw, not as instant market orders. Check the Pending tab and cancel any you no longer want.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/log-in.html","title":"Log In","text":""},{"location":"quick-start/log-in.html#log-in","title":"Log In","text":"<p>When you open ActTrader you see the login screen. You need three things from your broker: the server, your account ID and your password.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/log-in.html#log-in_1","title":"Log in","text":"<ol> <li>Click the Server box and type a few letters of your broker's name or server code. Matching servers appear as you type; live and demo servers are labelled, for example Fxview Live and Fxview Demo.</li> <li>Click your server in the list. (You can also use the Up and Down arrow keys and press Enter.)</li> <li>Enter your Account ID.</li> <li>Enter your Password. To check what you typed, click the eye button at the right of the box.</li> <li>Optional: tick Remember me to have your server, account ID and password filled in next time.</li> <li>Click Login.</li> </ol> <p>Your account, prices and chart load in a few seconds.</p> <p> </p> <p>The server search box, Account ID, Password, Remember me and the Login button. The gear at the top right opens settings you can change before logging in.</p> Watch how: Log in to ActTrader (0:51) <p></p> <p>Remember me on a shared computer</p> <p>Remember me stores your password on this computer. Do not use it on a computer other people can use.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/log-in.html#other-options-on-the-login-screen","title":"Other options on the login screen","text":"Option What it does Gear (top right) Settings you can change before logging in, such as a proxy or extra servers. See Settings Before You Log In. Forgot password? Opens your broker's password page in your browser. Register Opens your broker's sign-up page in your browser. Preview Opens a read-only demonstration session where trading is turned off. You are asked to confirm with Start Preview. <p>Forgot password?, Register and Preview appear only if your broker offers them.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/log-in.html#if-you-cannot-log-in","title":"If you cannot log in","text":"You see What to do Wrong Account Type or Username or Password Check the server, account ID and password. Passwords are case-sensitive. A message saying the broker's server had an error and it is not a credentials problem Your details are correct. The problem is on your broker's side, so contact your broker. Nothing happens, or the login times out Check your internet connection. If your network needs a proxy, set it up with the gear icon. <p>More help: Troubleshooting: Logging In.</p> <p>View-only accounts</p> <p>Some brokers issue view-only logins. You can log in and watch the account, but any attempt to trade is refused with a message saying the account is read-only.</p>"},{"location":"quick-start/settings-before-login.html","title":"Settings Before You Log In","text":""},{"location":"quick-start/settings-before-login.html#settings-before-you-log-in","title":"Settings Before You Log In","text":"<p>Some settings must be in place before you can connect, for example a proxy on a company network, or a server address your broker gave you that is not in the list. Click the gear at the top right of the login screen to change them.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Connection tab with the HTTP proxy and alternate server, and the Reset, Cancel and Save buttons.</p> Watch how: Settings on the login screen (0:32) <p></p> Watch how: Add a server and change language before login (0:27) <p></p>"},{"location":"quick-start/settings-before-login.html#the-tabs","title":"The tabs","text":"Tab What you can set Connection HTTP Proxy: tick Enable HTTP proxy for all network traffic and enter Host, Port, and (if needed) Username and Password. Alternate server (failover): a Host and Port to use if your main server cannot be reached. Language The language of the app. Theme Dark or Light. Entries Your own server entries. Enter a Name, URL and DB Alias and click Add. Remove one with its \u2715. <p>Click Save to keep your changes, Cancel to leave without saving, or Reset to go back to the defaults.</p> <p>Languages</p> <p>The list offers twenty languages, but only part of the app is translated so far. If you choose another language, many labels stay in English. Arabic and Hebrew switch the layout to right-to-left.</p>"},{"location":"summary/index.html","title":"The Summary Tab","text":""},{"location":"summary/index.html#the-summary-tab","title":"The Summary Tab","text":"<p>The Summary tab gathers five tables onto one screen so you can see your whole position at a glance. Drag the dividers between them to resize.</p> <p> </p> <p>Accounts across the top, aggregated Positions beneath, and Events and Messages, Risk Exposure and Price Alerts along the bottom.</p> Watch how: Summary at a glance (0:38) <p></p> Watch how: Use the Summary tab (1:12) <p></p>"},{"location":"summary/accounts.html","title":"Accounts","text":""},{"location":"summary/accounts.html#accounts","title":"Accounts","text":"<p>One row per account. If you have more than one account, an \"All\" row at the top adds them together and always stays first. Clicking a row selects that account, and the Positions table below then shows that account only. Clicking the All row shows every account again.</p> <p> </p> <p>One row per account, with an All row pinned at the top when you have more than one account.</p> Column Meaning Account Account identifier. The aggregate row reads All. Currency The account's base currency. AcT Account type. Owner The money owner's identifier. Balance Cash, excluding open positions. Equity Balance plus open profit and loss. Bonus Bonus amount. UsdMrgn Used Margin \u2014 collateral held against open positions. UsblMrgn Usable Margin \u2014 what is left to trade with. EqtyLevel% Equity as a percentage of Used Margin. Red below 100%, amber below 200%, green above. MC Margin call flag \u2014 Y or N. Y is shown in bold red. Mrgn Utiliz Used Margin as a percentage of Equity, as a bar. Amber from 80%, red from 100%. Dist to ME How far your equity is from the account's minimum equity requirement. OP Total open lots \u2014 the sum of your position sizes, not a count of positions. Com Commission, shown as a negative number. Roll Rollover interest. Net P/L Net profit or loss. DA Default amount percentage. Group The managed-account group this account belongs to, if any. A Whether the account is active for trading \u2014 Y or N. <p>The Bonus column's tooltip is wrong</p> <p>Hovering the Bonus header shows \"Price Shift\", which is left over from another column. The column itself does show the bonus amount.</p> <p>Right-click a row for: Select Account (followed by the account number), Select All Accounts, Summary by This Account, Summary by All Accounts, Closed Positions, MC Rates and Rollover Rates. The last two are greyed out unless your broker supplies the report links. \"Organize Managed Accounts\" is always greyed out and is not available in this release.</p> <p>Right-click the Accounts title bar for a shorter menu: Select All Accounts, Closed Positions, MC Rates and Rollover Rates.</p>"},{"location":"summary/events.html","title":"Events and Messages","text":""},{"location":"summary/events.html#events-and-messages","title":"Events and Messages","text":"<p>A timestamped log of what has happened \u2014 order fills, position changes and messages from your broker. The log is kept when you close and reopen the app. Three columns: Source, Message Title and Time. It is sorted newest first; click a header to sort by that column instead.</p> <p> </p> <p>The log, with the full text of the selected entry beneath.</p> <p>Colour in the Source column marks entries that need attention: EXCEPTION in red, SYSTEM and Warning in amber. Everything else is shown in normal text. Click a row to see the full text in the Details pane beneath; before you select anything it reads \"Select an event to view details\". When the log is empty it reads \"No events\".</p>"},{"location":"summary/export.html","title":"Exporting from Summary","text":""},{"location":"summary/export.html#exporting-from-summary","title":"Exporting from Summary","text":"<p>Press Alt+E to export whichever table has focus \u2014 Accounts and Positions export the positions summary, Events exports the event log, Alerts exports your alerts. With nothing focused, a message reads \"Alt+E \u2014 focus a list first\". There is also an Export CSV button on the Positions title bar, and Export to Excel\u2026 in the Positions right-click menu.</p> <p>Before anything is saved, an Export to CSV window shows which table will be saved and how many rows and columns it has. Click Export to save the file and open it in your spreadsheet app, or Cancel to stop.</p> <p> </p> <p>Shows the table name and its row and column count, with Cancel and Export buttons.</p> Watch how: Export a table to a spreadsheet (0:39) <p></p>"},{"location":"summary/positions.html","title":"Positions Summary","text":""},{"location":"summary/positions.html#positions-summary","title":"Positions Summary","text":"<p>This table aggregates your open positions \u2014 one row for each combination of instrument and side. An instrument with both Buy and Sell positions open therefore produces two rows.</p> <p> </p> <p>Open positions rolled up per instrument and side. The title states the scope, period and total, with a search box and Export CSV on the right.</p> Watch how: Use the Summary tab (1:12) <p></p> <p>The title bar summarises what you are looking at, for example: \"Summary \u2014 Account 100234 \u2014 Day \u2014 NH Only \u2014 (Net P/L == +$248.31)\". With every account included it reads \"All Accounts\" instead of the account number.</p> <p>To find an instrument quickly, type in the \"Search instrument\u2026\" box on the right of the title bar.</p> Watch how: Search and close from Summary (0:33) <p></p> Column Meaning Instrument The instrument. Lot Total size on this side. NH Lot The non-hedged part \u2014 how much is not cancelled out by the opposite side. B/S Buy or Sell. AvOpen Average price you opened at. AvClose Average price this side would close at now. AvBEP Average break-even price. Instrum P/L Combined profit or loss across both sides of this instrument. When both sides are open it is shown on one row only; the other row is left blank. P/L Profit or loss in pips. Net P/L Net profit or loss in money. Close A red Close button that closes every open position in this instrument \u2014 both Buy and Sell. NH P/L Profit or loss in pips on the non-hedged part only. NH Net P/L Net profit or loss on the non-hedged part only. <p>Right-click a row, the empty part of the table, or its title bar to change what is aggregated. Right-clicking the empty part is useful when every row is hidden \u2014 for example with Not hedged summary only switched on. Items that need a row (Close All, Copy Symbol) are greyed out when no row is selected.</p> Option group Choices Scope Summary by All accounts, or Summary by Selected accounts Period Overall Summary (every open position), Day Summary (positions opened in the broker's current trading day) or Shift Summary (positions opened in the broker's current shift) Filter Not hedged summary only (NH Mode) \u2014 hides rows that are fully hedged Table Filters (Hide Filters while they are showing), Clear All Filters Actions Close All for an instrument, Close All Buy for an instrument, Close All Sell for an instrument, Copy Symbol, Export to Excel\u2026 <p>The trading day ends at your broker's daily close time, and the shifts follow your broker's own shift times \u2014 not your computer's clock.</p> <p>Close All, the red Close button, double-clicking a row, and pressing Enter or Delete on a row all ask you to confirm, naming the instrument: \"Close all open positions for EURUSD at current market price?\" Click Close Positions to go ahead.</p> <p>Close All Buy and Close All Sell do not ask first</p> <p>These two items close the positions straight away, without a confirmation window.</p>"},{"location":"summary/price-alerts.html","title":"Price Alerts","text":""},{"location":"summary/price-alerts.html#price-alerts","title":"Price Alerts","text":"<p>Your active price alerts, under the heading Rate Alerts. Four columns: Instrument, B/S, C (the condition: &gt; for above, &lt; for below) and Rate. With no alerts it reads \"No alerts set\".</p> <p>Alerts are saved on your broker's server, so they are still there when you log in again. When the price reaches an alert, a notification appears and the alert is removed from the list.</p> <p> </p> <p>Active alerts, with the Chart Alerts section beneath.</p> Watch how: Manage price alerts (1:31) <p></p> <p>Right-click the list to manage your alerts:</p> Item What it does Add Alert Opens the alert window to create a new alert. Edit Alert Opens the selected alert so you can change it, then click Save. Double-clicking an alert does the same. Remove Alert Deletes the selected alert. You can also press the Delete key. Remove All Alerts Deletes every alert in the list. <p>Edit Alert and Remove Alert need a selected row. Remove Alert and Remove All Alerts ask you to confirm first; click Remove to go ahead.</p> <p>The B/S column shows Bid or Ask</p> <p>Although the header reads B/S and its tooltip says \"Buy / Sell\", the cells show which price the alert is watching \u2014 Bid or Ask.</p> <p>Chart Alerts is not available in this release</p> <p>Beneath Rate Alerts is a Chart Alerts section with four headings. It has no data behind it and always reads \"No chart alerts\".</p>"},{"location":"summary/risk.html","title":"Risk Exposure","text":""},{"location":"summary/risk.html#risk-exposure","title":"Risk Exposure","text":"<p>Your net exposure per currency, so that correlated risk across several pairs is visible. Three columns: Currency, Net Currency (exposure in currency units) and USD Value (the same converted to USD). A Buy and a Sell of the same size cancel each other out. With no open positions it reads \"No exposure\".</p> <p> </p> <p>Net exposure per currency across all open positions.</p>"},{"location":"tools/index.html","title":"Tools and Settings","text":""},{"location":"tools/index.html#tools-and-settings","title":"Tools and Settings","text":"<p>The features in this section behave the same way on every table and panel in the application.</p> Page The Command Palette Type an instruction with Ctrl+K Keyboard Use Moving around and working without the mouse Voice Commands Speak an instruction Sounds and Notifications Event sounds and pop-up messages Settings Every setting, tab by tab <p>Columns, sorting, filtering, export and floating windows are in Configuring Your Workspace. Default order distances are in the Trading Guide.</p>"},{"location":"tools/command-palette.html","title":"The Command Palette","text":""},{"location":"tools/command-palette.html#the-command-palette","title":"The Command Palette","text":"<p>Press Ctrl+K anywhere in the application to open the command palette, then type an instruction instead of hunting for the control. Press Ctrl+K again to close it.</p> <p> </p> <p>The palette listing its commands, each with the arguments it takes.</p> Watch how: Command palette, Help and sounds (1:07) <p></p> Command What it does Example buy Place a buy order. Add @ and a rate for an entry order, and sl or tp with a rate to attach a stop loss or take profit. buy 0.01 eurusd sell Place a sell order. Works the same way as buy. sell 0.10 gbpusd @ 1.2650 chart Open an instrument's chart on the Trading tab. chart gbpusd goto Switch to a workspace tab: trading, instruments, summary, reports, actfx, living or analytics. goto summary close Close all positions, only the profitable ones, or only the losing ones. close profitable alert Set a price alert on the Bid price. alert eurusd 1.1000 logout Sign out. logout <p>Typing just an instrument name, such as eurusd, opens its chart.</p> <p>Press Enter to run, Tab to complete, the arrow keys to move through the list, and Escape to close. A command that cannot be understood is refused with a message and the palette stays open.</p> <p>Palette orders and closes happen immediately</p> <p>A buy or sell typed here goes straight to your broker, with no Deal Ticket and no confirmation. The close commands also act at once. Typing close on its own, with nothing after it, closes all your positions.</p>"},{"location":"tools/keyboard.html","title":"Keyboard Use","text":""},{"location":"tools/keyboard.html#keyboard-use","title":"Keyboard Use","text":"<p>The application can be driven entirely from the keyboard. Tab and Shift+Tab move between the areas of the current tab; arrow keys move within a list; Enter acts on the highlighted row; Escape closes a dialog or clears a selection. Ctrl+Shift+Tab moves to the next workspace tab along the top.</p> <p>Shortcuts that act on a table only work while that table has focus, which prevents a keystroke meant for one panel affecting another. No shortcut fires while a dialog is open. Press Shift+F1 at any time for the full list \u2014 or open Help (?) at the bottom of the right-hand strip and choose Keyboard Shortcuts. Appendix B has the complete reference.</p> <p> </p> <p>Shift+F1 shows every shortcut, grouped by where it works.</p> Watch how: Use keyboard shortcuts (0:45) <p></p> <p>On macOS, Ctrl is shown as \u2318 and Alt as \u2325.</p>"},{"location":"tools/settings.html","title":"Settings","text":""},{"location":"tools/settings.html#settings","title":"Settings","text":"<p>The gear icon on the right-hand strip opens Settings. Five tabs are available to traders:</p> <p> </p> <p>The Settings window, showing the five tabs available to a trader.</p> Watch how: Use the settings icons (1:27) <p></p> Tab Contents Account Your Trader ID, Username and Currency; an Add Funds link if your broker provides one; the time zone used for all timestamps (My Computer, Server Time \u2014 your broker's server clock \u2014 or Custom, a zone you pick from a list); and the currency all money values are shown in. Security Change your password. Requirements are listed and ticked off as you type: minimum 8 characters, upper and lower case, at least one digit, at least one symbol. Diagnostics Collects system information, network tests, settings and logs to help support diagnose a problem. You choose what to include and whether to send it, save it to a file, or email it. Trading How sizes are shown (Full Amount, Amount, K, or Lots); Default Trader Range; Default Orders Distance per instrument (Configure\u2026); a confirmation prompt on exit; two-decimal currency display; the Show notifications switch; sounds; DDE publishing; and a Reset to defaults button. Session Your session details and a Log Out button. <p> </p> <p>Size display, trading defaults, exit confirmation, currency decimals, notifications and the sound options.</p> Watch how: Set time zone and trading defaults (0:45) <p></p> Watch how: Send a diagnostic report (0:36) <p></p> <p>Changes on the Trading tab apply straight away; there is no Save button.</p> <p>Reset to defaults also clears your order distances</p> <p>The Reset to defaults button at the bottom of the Trading tab sets sizes back to Lots and the Default Trader Range back to 10 pips. It also clears every custom default order distance. It acts at once, with no confirmation prompt.</p> <p>Theme, font size, panel visibility, profiles and news feeds are on the right-hand icon strip rather than in this window.</p>"},{"location":"tools/sounds.html","title":"Sounds and Notifications","text":""},{"location":"tools/sounds.html#sounds-and-notifications","title":"Sounds and Notifications","text":"<p>Settings \u2192 Trading has a master Enable sounds switch, a Volume slider, and individual switches for Order placed, Order filled, Position closed, Order rejected / failed, Price alert triggered, Margin call, and Feed / connection lost. Each event plays its own short sound.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Show notifications switch, the Enable sounds switch, the Volume slider and one switch for each event.</p> Watch how: Set time zone and trading defaults (0:45) <p></p> Watch how: Command palette, Help and sounds (1:07) <p></p> <p>Above the sound options, the Show notifications switch turns pop-up messages and event sounds off together. While it is off, Enable sounds reads \"Currently silenced by the Notifications switch above\". Margin calls are always shown, and the event log keeps recording everything.</p> <p>If your build has no audio support, Settings shows: \"Audio backend unavailable in this build\" and no sound will play.</p>"},{"location":"tools/voice.html","title":"Voice Commands","text":""},{"location":"tools/voice.html#voice-commands","title":"Voice Commands","text":"<p>If voice is available for your account, a microphone button appears on the right-hand strip while you are connected. Click it to open the Voice Assistant and speak. The status line reads \"Listening \u2014 speak now\u2026\", then \"Transcribing\u2026\", then \"Thinking\u2026\".</p> <p> </p> <p>What you said, the assistant's reply, and the mic, sound and hands-free buttons.</p> <p>You can ask questions about your account, open a tab or a chart (for example \"Open EURUSD chart\"), or give instructions: place an order, close a position, cancel a pending order, set a stop or limit, close all positions, cancel all orders, close only the profitable or losing ones, or close everything on one instrument.</p> <p>Every instruction is shown for confirmation before anything happens. Instructions that affect everything at once \u2014 close all positions, cancel all orders \u2014 require a second confirmation, which spells out what is about to happen and warns that it cannot be undone.</p> <p>The assistant also reads its answers aloud. Use the speaker button at the top of the panel to mute or unmute it.</p> <p>Hands-free mode is off until you switch it on with its button at the top of the panel. While it is on, say the wake phrase \"Hey ActTrader\" to start listening without clicking.</p> <p>If the feature cannot run, the panel explains why: \"Voice input unavailable\" (no audio support in this build), \"Voice recognition not configured\", or \"No microphone detected\". The last two have a Retry button.</p>"},{"location":"trading/index.html","title":"Trading Guide","text":""},{"location":"trading/index.html#trading-guide","title":"Trading Guide","text":"<p>This guide shows you how to place, protect, change and close your trades. Each page covers one task, with step-by-step instructions, a screenshot and a short video.</p> I want to\u2026 Read Buy or sell now, at the current price Open a New Position (Market Order) Buy or sell later, when the price reaches my level Entry Orders Catch a move in either direction with one order OCO Orders Limit my loss or lock in my profit Stop Loss and Take Profit Change or cancel an order that is waiting Change or Cancel a Pending Order Take my profit or loss, or protect a trade with a hedge Close and Hedge Positions Trade with a single click, without the order ticket One-Click Trading (Quick Trade) Be told when a price reaches a level Price Alerts Set my usual stop, limit and entry distances Default Order Distances Look up a field or a message in the order ticket Deal Ticket Reference <p>Orders are sent as soon as you confirm</p> <p>When you click Buy or Sell in the Deal Ticket, or Ok in a stop, limit or close window, the instruction goes to your broker straight away. The app never sends the same instruction twice while it waits for a reply, so a double-click cannot place two orders.</p>"},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html","title":"Close and Hedge Positions","text":""},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#close-and-hedge-positions","title":"Close and Hedge Positions","text":""},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#close-a-position","title":"Close a position","text":"<ol> <li>On the Open tab, click the \u2715 at the end of the trade's row. You can also right-click the trade and choose Close Position, or select it and press Alt+C.</li> <li>The Close Position window opens, showing which trade you are closing. To close all of it, leave the Amount as it is.</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>The trade is removed from the Open tab. You can see it, with its final profit or loss, on the Closed tab.</p> <p> </p> <p>The amount to close with its slider, the rate, and Use current dealing rate.</p> Watch how: Close a position (0:52) <p></p> <p>Close from the chart</p> <p>Click the X on a trade's line on the chart. The Close Position window opens in the same way. See Trading from the chart.</p> Watch how: Close a trade from the chart (0:35) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#close-part-of-a-position","title":"Close part of a position","text":"<ol> <li>Open the Close Position window as above.</li> <li>Change the Amount to the part you want to close, or drag the slider.</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>The rest of the trade stays open with the smaller amount.</p> Watch how: Close part of a position (0:34) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#the-close-position-window","title":"The Close Position window","text":"Field What it means Amount How much to close. The whole position to start with. Rate The price to close at. It follows the live price while Use current dealing rate is ticked. Use current dealing rate Ticked: close at the live price. Untick it to type your own price. Price Shift Not used in this version. Leave it at 0. <p>If no live price has arrived yet, the window shows \"No live price for\" the instrument and waits. The rate fills in as soon as a price arrives.</p> <p>Quick Trade closes at once</p> <p>With Quick Trade switched on, the \u2715 button and Close Position close the trade immediately, without this window. See One-Click Trading.</p>"},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#close-several-positions-at-once","title":"Close several positions at once","text":"<p>Use Bulk Operations above the Open tab to close all positions, only the profitable ones, or only the losing ones. You are asked to confirm first. More choices (by side or by instrument) are in the right-click menu under Bulk Operations.</p> Watch how: Close several positions at once (0:31) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/close-and-hedge.html#hedge-a-position","title":"Hedge a position","text":"<p>A hedge opens a trade of the same size on the opposite side. While you hold both, price moves no longer change your total profit or loss.</p> <ol> <li>Click the H next to the trade on the Open tab. You can also right-click it and choose Hedge Position, or press Alt+H.</li> <li>The Deal Ticket opens already set up: the opposite side, the same amount, and a comment that links it to the original trade (\"Hedge of TradeId [number]\").</li> <li>Click Buy or Sell to open the hedge.</li> </ol> Watch how: Quick order and hedge (0:41) <p></p> <p>Preset Stop and Preset Limit are ignored when hedging</p> <p>You can fill them in, but they are not sent with a hedge. Add a stop or limit to the new trade afterwards.</p>"},{"location":"trading/deal-ticket-reference.html","title":"Deal Ticket Reference","text":""},{"location":"trading/deal-ticket-reference.html#deal-ticket-reference","title":"Deal Ticket Reference","text":"<p>This page lists every field, button and message in the Deal Ticket. For step-by-step instructions, see Open a New Position, Entry Orders and OCO Orders.</p>"},{"location":"trading/deal-ticket-reference.html#order-types","title":"Order types","text":"<p>The four tabs at the top of the ticket. Ctrl+Tab moves between them.</p> Tab What it does When it trades Market Buys or sells straight away at the price shown. Immediately. Limit Waits for a better price: buys lower, sells higher. When the market reaches your rate. Entry Waits for the market to move your way: buys higher, sells lower. When the market reaches your rate. OCO Places a Stop and a Limit together; the first to trade cancels the other. When either one is reached."},{"location":"trading/deal-ticket-reference.html#fields","title":"Fields","text":"Field What it is Starts at Accepts Buy / Sell Which way you are trading. Alt+B and Alt+S also switch it. The side you clicked \u2014 Amount The trade size. Its label follows your size setting: Amount (Lots), Amount, or Amount, K. A size suited to your account, never below the instrument's minimum Up to 8 decimals; a trailing K is accepted Rate The order price. On the Market tab it follows the live price and cannot be edited. The current Bid or Ask Up to 6 decimals Distance in pips Limit and Entry only. How far from the market the order waits; it stays in step with Rate. Your default entry distance, never below your broker's minimum Up to 1 decimal Trader Range Market only. How many pips the price may move against you and still fill. 0 = exact price only. Your Default Trader Range setting Whole numbers Preset Stop Attach a stop loss that starts working when the order fills. Adds Rate, Distance in pips and Projected P/L fields. Off; when ticked, your default stop distance Tick box Trailing Distance Makes the preset stop follow the price. Appears when Preset Stop is ticked. Off Tick box Preset Limit Attach a take profit that starts working when the order fills. Off; when ticked, your default limit distance Tick box Comment Your own note, saved with the trade. Empty Up to 100 characters <ul> <li>\u2212 and +, or the Up and Down arrow keys, change the amount. The arrows beside the rate boxes change a price.</li> <li>The slider covers the usual range of sizes; to trade more, type the size.</li> <li>Preset Stop and Preset Limit are not available on the OCO tab.</li> <li>The two large buttons at the bottom place the order and show the side and price, for example Buy 1.08432. Enter places the order on the side selected.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"trading/deal-ticket-reference.html#messages-you-may-see","title":"Messages you may see","text":"<p>While you fill in the ticket, an amber line with a \u26a0 explains anything that is wrong, and the Buy and Sell buttons stay dimmed until it is fixed.</p> Message What it means What to do Enter a rate The Rate box is empty or zero. Type a price. Rate must be below current ask A Buy Limit must be below the market. Lower the rate, or click Use this. Rate must be above current bid A Sell Limit must be above the market. Raise the rate. Rate must be at least 10 pips from market Your broker does not accept orders closer than this (the number varies). Move the rate further away. Nearest valid: 1.08432 The closest price your broker accepts. Click Use this to fill it in. OCO stop must be above ask The Stop rate is on the wrong side. Raise the Stop Rate. OCO limit must be below ask The Limit rate is on the wrong side. Lower the Limit Rate. OCO stop (or limit) must be at least 10 pips from market That rate is too close to the market. Move it further away. <p>After you click Buy or Sell, the line shows Placing order\u2026 (or Placing OCO order\u2026 / Placing hedge order\u2026). The ticket then closes, or your broker's reason for refusing the order appears in red. A Copy button copies that message, for example to send to support.</p> <p>On a small window</p> <p>The Deal Ticket has a fixed width. If your window is very narrow, part of it can be cut off; make the window wider. On a short window the ticket scrolls.</p>"},{"location":"trading/entry-orders.html","title":"Entry Orders","text":""},{"location":"trading/entry-orders.html#entry-orders","title":"Entry Orders","text":"<p>An entry order waits and only trades when the price reaches the level you choose. Until then it is a pending order, listed on the Pending tab.</p>"},{"location":"trading/entry-orders.html#which-entry-order-to-use","title":"Which entry order to use","text":"You want to\u2026 Use It trades when\u2026 Buy cheaper than now Limit Buy the price falls to your rate Sell higher than now Limit Sell the price rises to your rate Buy if the price breaks upwards Entry (Stop) Buy the price rises to your rate Sell if the price breaks downwards Entry (Stop) Sell the price falls to your rate Watch how: Entry Stop vs Entry Limit (0:54)"},{"location":"trading/entry-orders.html#place-an-entry-order","title":"Place an entry order","text":"<ol> <li>Right-click the instrument in the watchlist and choose Entry Limit Buy, Entry Limit Sell, Entry Stop Buy or Entry Stop Sell. The Deal Ticket opens on the matching tab.</li> <li>Set how far from the current price the order should wait, in Distance in pips. The Rate updates to match. You can type the rate instead; the distance follows.</li> <li>Set the Amount.</li> <li>Optional: tick Preset Stop and/or Preset Limit to protect the trade as soon as the order fills.</li> <li>Click Buy or Sell.</li> </ol> <p>The order now waits on the Pending tab until the price reaches it, or until you cancel it.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Deal Ticket on the Limit tab: Distance in pips sits beside Rate, and the two stay in step as you type.</p> Watch how: Place a pending (limit) order (0:43) <p></p> <p>Other ways</p> <p>Open the Deal Ticket any way you like (for example by clicking a price) and click the Limit or Entry tab. Ctrl+Tab moves between the tabs.</p> <p>Your rate stays where you set it</p> <p>The rate starts at your default entry distance from the market (see Default Order Distances). Once set, it does not move with the market while the ticket is open, so the price you see is the price that is sent.</p> <p>If the rate is on the wrong side of the market, or closer than your broker allows, an amber message explains why and the Buy and Sell buttons stay dimmed. See Messages you may see.</p> <p>To change or cancel the order later, see Change or Cancel a Pending Order.</p>"},{"location":"trading/market-order.html","title":"Open a New Position (Market Order)","text":""},{"location":"trading/market-order.html#open-a-new-position-market-order","title":"Open a New Position (Market Order)","text":"<p>A market order buys or sells straight away at the current price. You place it from the Deal Ticket.</p>"},{"location":"trading/market-order.html#place-a-market-order","title":"Place a market order","text":"<ol> <li>In the watchlist, click the Ask price of the instrument to buy, or the Bid price to sell. The Deal Ticket opens on the Market tab.</li> <li>Check the side. Buy or Sell is highlighted at the top; click the other one to change it.</li> <li>Set the Amount. Use \u2212 and +, drag the slider, or type a size.</li> <li>Optional: tick Preset Stop and/or Preset Limit to add a stop loss or take profit now. You can also add them later.</li> <li>Click the large Buy or Sell button at the bottom. It shows the price you will trade at.</li> </ol> <p>Your new position appears straight away on the Open tab at the bottom of the screen.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Deal Ticket on the Market tab, set to Buy, with the live Sell and Buy prices, the amount and the Trader Range.</p> Watch how: Quick order and hedge (0:41) <p></p> Watch how: Place a market order (0:46) <p></p> <p>Other ways to open the Deal Ticket</p> <ul> <li>Select an instrument and press Alt+B to buy or Alt+S to sell.</li> <li>Right-click an instrument and choose Market Order Buy or Market Order Sell.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"trading/market-order.html#what-you-see-in-the-ticket","title":"What you see in the ticket","text":"Item What it means Sell / Buy prices The live prices. You buy at the Buy (Ask) price and sell at the Sell (Bid) price. Amount (Lots) How much to trade. It starts at a size suited to your account, and never below the instrument's minimum. Rate The price of the order. On the Market tab it follows the live price and cannot be edited. Trader Range How many pips the price may move against you and the order still fills. 0 means only at the exact price. Preset Stop / Preset Limit Attach a stop loss or take profit that starts working as soon as the order fills. Comment Your own note, saved with the trade. <p>For every field and message, see the Deal Ticket Reference.</p> <p>The Buy/Sell strip above the chart trades at once</p> <p>The SELL and BUY buttons above the chart place a market order immediately, at the size in the strip's lot box, without opening the Deal Ticket. See The Chart.</p> <p>With Quick Trade on, there is no ticket</p> <p>If Quick Trade is switched on, clicking a Bid or Ask price trades immediately at the size in that row, without opening the Deal Ticket. See One-Click Trading.</p>"},{"location":"trading/modify-cancel-order.html","title":"Change or Cancel a Pending Order","text":""},{"location":"trading/modify-cancel-order.html#change-or-cancel-a-pending-order","title":"Change or Cancel a Pending Order","text":"<p>A pending order can be changed or cancelled at any time before it trades.</p>"},{"location":"trading/modify-cancel-order.html#change-an-order","title":"Change an order","text":"<ol> <li>On the Pending tab, right-click the order and choose Modify Order. You can also click the \u270e button on its row, or select it and press Alt+M.</li> <li>Enter a new Entry Rate and/or Amount.</li> <li>Click Modify.</li> </ol> <p>The message Order modified confirms the change, and the new rate shows in the Rate column.</p> <p> </p> <p>The order's instrument and type at the top, with the Entry Rate and Amount you can change.</p> Watch how: Change or cancel a pending order (0:52) <p></p> <p>The same rules as a new order apply: if the rate is on the wrong side of the market or too close to it, an amber message explains why and Modify stays greyed out. When the app can suggest the nearest acceptable rate, a Use this button fills it in for you.</p>"},{"location":"trading/modify-cancel-order.html#cancel-an-order","title":"Cancel an order","text":"<ol> <li>On the Pending tab, right-click the order and choose Remove Order. You can also click the \u2715 on its row, or select it and press Alt+R or Delete.</li> <li>Confirm when asked.</li> </ol> <p>The order is cancelled and removed from the Pending tab.</p> <p> </p> <p>Right-click a pending order to modify or remove it, attach a stop or limit, add a comment, or cancel many orders at once.</p>"},{"location":"trading/modify-cancel-order.html#cancel-several-orders-at-once","title":"Cancel several orders at once","text":"<p>Right-click any order and open Bulk Operations. You can cancel all orders, or only limit or stop orders. You are shown how many orders will be cancelled and asked to confirm.</p> Watch how: Pending-order menu and bulk cancel (0:54) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/oco-orders.html","title":"OCO Orders","text":""},{"location":"trading/oco-orders.html#oco-orders","title":"OCO Orders","text":"<p>OCO means One Cancels the Other. It places two entry orders at once, a Stop and a Limit. As soon as one of them trades, the other is cancelled automatically. Use it when you want to trade the next move, whichever way it goes.</p>"},{"location":"trading/oco-orders.html#place-an-oco-order","title":"Place an OCO order","text":"<ol> <li>Right-click the instrument in the watchlist and choose Entry OCO Buy or Entry OCO Sell. The Deal Ticket opens on the OCO tab.</li> <li>Set the Stop Rate and the Limit Rate (see the table below). Both start at your broker's minimum distance from the market.</li> <li>Set the Amount.</li> <li>Click Buy or Sell. Both orders are placed together and wait on the Pending tab.</li> </ol> <p>The OCO tab with the Stop Rate and Limit Rate, each with the closest price your broker accepts shown beneath it.</p> Watch how: Place an OCO order (0:41) <p></p> Field For a Buy For a Sell Stop Rate Above the Ask: buys if the price breaks upwards. Below the Bid: sells if the price breaks downwards. Limit Rate Below the Ask: buys if the price dips. Above the Bid: sells if the price rallies. <p>The closest allowed price is shown under each field, for example &gt;= 1.08432. If you enter a rate on the wrong side of the market, or too close to it, it is moved to the nearest allowed price when you leave the field.</p> <p>Note</p> <p>Preset Stop and Preset Limit are not available on the OCO tab.</p>"},{"location":"trading/one-click-trading.html","title":"One-Click Trading (Quick Trade)","text":""},{"location":"trading/one-click-trading.html#one-click-trading-quick-trade","title":"One-Click Trading (Quick Trade)","text":"<p>With Quick Trade switched on, a single click on a price trades immediately, without opening the Deal Ticket. Use it when speed matters.</p>"},{"location":"trading/one-click-trading.html#turn-quick-trade-on","title":"Turn Quick Trade on","text":"<ol> <li>Click the \u21af button at the right of the watchlist's search box, or press Alt+Q. The button is highlighted while Quick Trade is on.</li> <li>A LOT box with \u2212 and + appears on every watchlist row. Set the size you want to trade for each instrument.</li> </ol> <p>The \u21af button highlighted, and a lot box with \u2212 and + on every watchlist row.</p> Watch how: Trade with one click (Quick Trade) (0:45) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/one-click-trading.html#trade-with-one-click","title":"Trade with one click","text":"<ul> <li>Click the Ask price to buy at once.</li> <li>Click the Bid price to sell at once.</li> <li>Alt+B and Alt+S also trade at once.</li> </ul> <p>The trade uses the size in that row's lot box. The new position appears on the Open tab straight away.</p> <p>There is no confirmation</p> <p>With Quick Trade on, every click on a price sends a live order, and Close Position (or the \u2715 on a trade) closes it immediately without the Close Position window. Turn Quick Trade off with the \u21af button or Alt+Q when you are not using it.</p>"},{"location":"trading/one-click-trading.html#turn-quick-trade-off","title":"Turn Quick Trade off","text":"<p>Click the \u21af button again, or press Alt+Q. Clicking a price then opens the Deal Ticket as usual.</p>"},{"location":"trading/order-distances.html","title":"Default Order Distances","text":""},{"location":"trading/order-distances.html#default-order-distances","title":"Default Order Distances","text":"<p>You can set, for each instrument, how far from the market new stops, limits and entry orders start. These are the distances the order windows fill in for you.</p>"},{"location":"trading/order-distances.html#change-a-distance","title":"Change a distance","text":"<ol> <li>Open Settings (the gear on the right), go to the Trading tab, and under Default Orders Distance click Configure\u2026.</li> <li>Find the instrument. The search box at the top filters the list.</li> <li>Click its STOP, LIMIT or ENTRY cell, type the distance in pips, and confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Every instrument with its Stop, Limit and Entry defaults beside the broker's minimum distance.</p> Watch how: Set default order distances (0:50) <p></p> <p>Change many instruments at once</p> <p>Tick several rows first. One edit then applies to all of them, and a message confirms how many were updated.</p>"},{"location":"trading/order-distances.html#what-the-table-shows","title":"What the table shows","text":"Column What it shows INSTRUMENT The instrument. STOP Your default stop loss distance, in pips. LIMIT Your default take profit distance, in pips. ENTRY Your default entry-order distance, in pips. MIN. DISTANCE The closest your broker accepts. You cannot change it. <p>A value in grey follows your broker's minimum. A value in bold is one you set. A dash means no distance is set.</p>"},{"location":"trading/order-distances.html#rules","title":"Rules","text":"<ul> <li>A distance must be more than your broker's minimum. If it isn't, it is not saved and you see \"Not saved \u2014 broker minimum is \u2026 pips for this instrument\".</li> <li>Enter 0 to go back to the broker's minimum.</li> </ul> <p>Resetting cannot be undone</p> <p>Reset all distances to default, and Reset to defaults on the Settings \u2192 Trading tab, clear your custom distances for every instrument at once, with no confirmation.</p>"},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html","title":"Price Alerts","text":""},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html#price-alerts","title":"Price Alerts","text":"<p>A price alert tells you when an instrument's price reaches a level you choose. Your alerts are kept on your broker's server, so they are still there the next time you log in.</p>"},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html#set-an-alert","title":"Set an alert","text":"<ol> <li>In the watchlist, point at the instrument and click the \u25b3 that appears on its row. You can also select it and press Alt+P, or right-click it and choose Price Alert.</li> <li>Under Watch Price, choose Bid or Ask: the price to watch.</li> <li>Set the Alert Rate. It starts at the current price. Type the price you want, or use the arrows.</li> <li>Read the line under the rate. It tells you what will trigger the alert, for example \"Bid rises to 1.08500\".</li> <li>Click Set Alert.</li> </ol> <p>The instrument with its live Bid and Ask, the Bid/Ask choice, the Alert Rate and the line that says what will trigger the alert.</p> Watch how: Set a price alert (0:46) <p></p> <p>You don't choose \"above\" or \"below\": the app works this out from where your rate is compared with the current price.</p>"},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html#when-an-alert-is-reached","title":"When an alert is reached","text":"<p>A notification appears, and the alert is removed from your list. An alert set at the current price is reached almost at once.</p>"},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html#see-and-manage-your-alerts","title":"See and manage your alerts","text":"<p>Your alerts are listed on the Summary tab, under Price Alerts. Right-click the list:</p> Choice What it does Add Alert Create a new alert. Type the instrument and pick it from the list. Edit Alert Change an alert's rate, then click Save. Double-clicking an alert does the same. Remove Alert Delete one alert, after you confirm. Remove All Alerts Clear the whole list, after you confirm. <p> </p> <p>Your alerts on the Summary tab, showing the instrument, Bid or Ask, the direction (&gt; above, &lt; below) and the rate.</p> Watch how: Manage price alerts (1:31) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/price-alerts.html#messages-you-may-see","title":"Messages you may see","text":"Message What it means Enter a valid rate The rate box is empty or zero. Choose an instrument from the list The name typed is not an instrument your broker offers. Price alerts are not available right now Your broker's alert service cannot be reached. Try again later. This alert has already triggered The alert was reached while you were editing it."},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html","title":"Stop Loss and Take Profit","text":""},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#stop-loss-and-take-profit","title":"Stop Loss and Take Profit","text":"<ul> <li>A stop loss (Stop) closes your trade automatically if the price moves against you, so your loss cannot grow past the level you set.</li> <li>A take profit (Limit) closes your trade automatically when the price reaches your target, locking in the gain.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#set-a-stop-loss","title":"Set a stop loss","text":"<ol> <li>On the Open tab, right-click the trade and choose Stop (Set SL). You can also click the trade's Stop cell, or select it and press Alt+T.</li> <li>Enter the Rate: the price at which you want to get out. The live price is shown beside it. Distance in points shows the same level as a distance from the market, and Projected P/L shows what you would lose if the stop is hit.</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>The stop now shows in the trade's Stop column.</p> <p> </p> <p>Rate with the live price beside it, Distance in points, Projected P/L and the Set Trailing Stop Distance option.</p> Watch how: Set a stop loss and take profit (0:57) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#set-a-take-profit","title":"Set a take profit","text":"<ol> <li>Right-click the trade and choose Limit (Set TP). You can also click its Limit cell, or press Alt+L.</li> <li>Enter the Rate of your target. Projected P/L shows what you would make.</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>The same layout as Stop Loss; the rate sits on the other side of the market and the projected figure is a gain.</p> <p>Faster: drag it on the chart</p> <p>You can also add, move and remove a stop loss or take profit by dragging its line on the chart, then clicking the tick to save. See Trading from the chart.</p> Watch how: Move stop loss / take profit on the chart (0:41) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#use-a-trailing-stop","title":"Use a trailing stop","text":"<p>A trailing stop follows the price as it moves in your favour, staying the same distance behind it. It never moves back.</p> <ol> <li>Right-click the trade and choose Trailing Stop. The Stop Loss window opens with Set Trailing Stop Distance already ticked.</li> <li>Enter how far behind the price the stop should follow (at least 1.0).</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>The trailing distance shows in the trade's TR.STOP column.</p> <p>Note</p> <p>When Set Trailing Stop Distance is ticked, the stop is placed using the trailing distance only. The Rate box is not used.</p> Watch how: Use a trailing stop (0:43) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#remove-a-stop-loss-or-take-profit","title":"Remove a stop loss or take profit","text":"<p>Open the same window and click Remove.</p> <p>Remove acts immediately</p> <p>There is no confirmation. The stop loss or take profit is deleted as soon as you click Remove, and the trade is no longer protected at that level.</p> Watch how: Remove a stop loss or take profit (0:39) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#add-them-to-a-pending-order","title":"Add them to a pending order","text":"<p>You can protect an entry order before it fills. On the Pending tab, right-click the order and choose Stop (Pre-defined SL), Limit (Pre-defined TP) or Trailing Stop. The same windows open, but the distance and Projected P/L are measured from the price the order will fill at, not from today's price.</p> Watch how: Pending-order menu and bulk cancel (0:54) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading/stop-and-limit.html#messages-you-may-see","title":"Messages you may see","text":"Message What it means Stop loss must be below current bid On a Buy trade the stop must be below the market. Stop loss must be above current ask On a Sell trade the stop must be above the market. Take profit must be above current ask On a Buy trade the target must be above the market. Take profit must be below current bid On a Sell trade the target must be below the market. Stop must be at least 2.0 pips from market Your broker's minimum distance for this instrument (the number varies). Invalid rate The Rate box is empty or zero. Stop loss updated / Take profit placed Done. The window closes shortly after. <p>For a pending order the messages refer to the order instead, for example \"Stop loss must be below the order's fill price\".</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/index.html","title":"The Trading Tab","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/index.html#the-trading-tab","title":"The Trading Tab","text":"<p>The Trading tab is your main screen. It has four areas:</p> <ul> <li>the watchlist of live prices on the left,</li> <li>the chart in the centre, with the Buy/Sell strip above it,</li> <li>the news on the right,</li> <li>your Open, Pending and Closed trades along the bottom.</li> </ul> <p>Drag the dividers between the areas to resize them; the sizes are remembered. You can switch the news panel off from Panels on the right-hand icon strip.</p> <p> </p> <p>The watchlist on the left, the chart with the Buy/Sell strip in the centre, news on the right, and the Open / Pending / Closed tables at the bottom.</p> Watch how: Read the chart (0:52) <p></p> Read about Chart Controls New chart, Linked, the chart layout and turning charts off The Watchlist Live prices, your own watchlists, and trading from the list The Chart Your trades on the chart, and the Buy/Sell strip Open Positions Your open trades and what you can do with them Pending Orders Orders waiting for their price Closed Positions Your trading history The Account Status Bar Balance, equity and margin at a glance"},{"location":"trading-tab/chart-controls.html","title":"Chart Controls","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/chart-controls.html#chart-controls","title":"Chart Controls","text":"<p>The chart controls sit at the right end of the tab row, and only appear on the Trading tab. On a narrow window they fold away behind a \u2039 button: click it to show them, and click it again (or press Escape) to hide them.</p> <p> </p> <p>New chart, Linked, the layout picker and the charts on/off button.</p> Watch how: Show several charts at once (1:08) <p></p> Control What it does + New chart Opens the current instrument in its own chart window. You can have up to six; at the limit the button is greyed out (\"Chart window limit reached (6)\"). See Floating Windows. Linked On (the default): choosing an instrument in the watchlist changes every chart. Off: it changes only the chart you last clicked. Layout How many charts to show at once: one, two side by side, two stacked, four, six or nine. The current layout is ticked. \u25a6 Turns all charts off, or back on. With charts off, the chart area is unloaded to save memory and processor time, and chart windows are closed. Watch how: Pop out charts and panels (0:40) <p></p> <p>Two-chart layouts: read the words, not the numbers</p> <p>In the layout menu, the numbers of the two-chart options don't match the numbers shown on the button afterwards. Choosing \"2\u00d71 \u2014 2 charts side by side\" shows 1\u00d72 on the button, and \"1\u00d72 \u2014 2 charts stacked\" shows 2\u00d71. The words after the dash are correct.</p> <p>Turning charts back on does not reopen chart windows that were closed; use + New chart to open them again.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/chart.html","title":"The Chart","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/chart.html#the-chart","title":"The Chart","text":"<p>The chart area shows one to nine charts, depending on the layout you choose with the chart controls. Your open positions and pending orders are drawn on the chart as lines with labels. For everything about candles, timeframes, indicators and drawing, see Charts.</p> Watch how: Read the chart (0:52) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/chart.html#your-trades-on-the-chart","title":"Your trades on the chart","text":"<p>Each open position is a line at its opening price; its label shows the side, size and profit or loss.</p> <ul> <li>Set or move a stop loss / take profit: click the position's label, drag SL or TP to the price you want (the label shows the profit or loss at that price), then click the tick to save.</li> <li>Close a position: click the \u2715 on its label. The Close Position window opens first, so nothing closes until you confirm. (With Quick Trade on, it closes at once.)</li> <li>Place an order at a price: point at the price and click the + at the right edge, then choose the order type. A draft line appears; nothing is sent until you confirm it.</li> </ul> <p> </p> <p>An open position drawn as a line, with its label showing the side, size and profit or loss.</p> Watch how: Move stop loss / take profit on the chart (0:41) <p></p> Watch how: Close a trade from the chart (0:35) <p></p> Watch how: Place an order from the chart (0:51) <p></p> <p>Press Escape while the chart has focus to undo a stop or limit change you have dragged but not saved.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/chart.html#the-buysell-strip","title":"The Buy/Sell strip","text":"<p>Above the chart (when one chart is shown, or one chart of a grid is made full size) is a compact trading strip.</p> <p> </p> <p>SELL with the Bid price, the lot size with arrows, BUY with the Ask price, and the spread.</p> Watch how: One-click Buy/Sell above the chart (0:28) <p></p> Control What it does SELL (Bid price) Sells at once at the size in the lot box. Lot box The size to trade. Use the arrows, the mouse wheel or Up/Down; double-click to type a size. BUY (Ask price) Buys at once. SPRD The current spread; point at it to see the full value. <p>The strip trades immediately</p> <p>SELL and BUY send the order straight away, with no Deal Ticket and no confirmation. Check the size in the lot box before you click.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/chart.html#the-charts-right-click-menu","title":"The chart's right-click menu","text":"Item What it does Undock this chart Move this chart into its own window. <p>To reuse a set of indicators on other charts, use an indicator template. Chart colours and other settings can be saved as a template in Chart Settings.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/closed-positions.html","title":"Closed Positions","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/closed-positions.html#closed-positions","title":"Closed Positions","text":"<p>The Closed tab shows the trades you have closed, with their open and close prices and the final profit or loss.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/closed-positions.html#choose-how-far-back-to-look","title":"Choose how far back to look","text":"<ol> <li>Click the period button on the Closed tab's toolbar. It shows the period currently loaded.</li> <li>In Show Closed Trades, pick 1 Day (the standard), 5 Days, 1 Month, 6 Months or Custom.</li> <li>For Custom, enter the From and Till dates and times and click Show Result.</li> </ol> <p>The period choices, with From and Till for a custom range.</p> Watch how: Close a position (0:52) <p></p> <p>If there are no closed trades in the period, the table says so, with a Widen the period to see older trades link.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/closed-positions.html#the-columns","title":"The columns","text":"<p>The Closed table has the same columns as Open Positions, with Close (the price you closed at) and Close Time instead of the live figures. You can also turn on Cl. Charge, Duration, User, Closed By and Reason (why it closed, for example S stop loss, L take profit, M margin call) with Customize\u2026. A dash in Reason means you closed the trade yourself.</p> Watch how: Closed trades for any period (0:47) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/closed-positions.html#right-click-menu-and-keys","title":"Right-click menu and keys","text":"<p>Right-click a row for Copy Trade ID, View on Chart, Export to Excel\u2026 and the filter items.</p> Keys What they do Up / Down, Home / End Move through the rows. Ctrl+C Copy the highlighted trade's reference. Alt+E Export to CSV. <p>You can sort, filter and export closed trades like any other table. See Sorting, Filtering and Export to CSV.</p> Watch how: Sort and filter a table (0:53) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html","title":"Open Positions","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#open-positions","title":"Open Positions","text":"<p>The Open tab at the bottom of the Trading tab lists your open trades with their live profit or loss. The number on the tab shows how many you have.</p> <p> </p> <p>The toolbar above the table, and an open position with its H and \u2715 buttons at the right.</p> Watch how: Read the positions table (1:50) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#what-you-can-do-with-a-position","title":"What you can do with a position","text":"To\u2026 Do this Set a stop loss or take profit Click its Stop or Limit cell. See Stop Loss and Take Profit. Close it Click the \u2715 at the right of the row. See Close and Hedge Positions. Hedge it Click the H at the right of the row. See it on the chart Click the instrument name. Anything else Right-click the row (see below)."},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#the-toolbar","title":"The toolbar","text":"Control What it does Size The total size of all your open positions. Grouped / Ungrouped One row per trade (Ungrouped, the default) or one row per instrument (Grouped). Bulk Operations \u25be Close all positions, only the profitable ones, or only the losing ones. You are asked to confirm. Unrealised P/L The live profit or loss of all your open positions. A \u26a0 means some could not be included because a conversion rate is missing. Filters Show the filter row. See Filtering. Export CSV Save the table to a spreadsheet. See Export to CSV. Watch how: Close several positions at once (0:31)"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#grouped-view","title":"Grouped view","text":"<p>Turn on Grouped to see one row per instrument instead of one per trade. The row shows the total size and the average open price (marked \u2248). Click the arrow on a grouped row to show the trades inside it, and again to hide them.</p> <p> </p> <p>One row per instrument, with the average open price marked \u2248.</p> Watch how: Group positions by instrument (0:38) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#the-columns","title":"The columns","text":"<p>These columns are shown as standard. Right-click a heading and choose Customize\u2026 to show others (Currency, Lot P/L, BEP, Fee, Opn Charge, Prm, Fut Roll Adj, Admin Fee, Trade Open Time, Opened By, PrOrd, Trade ID, Comment).</p> Column What it shows Account The account holding the position. Instrument The instrument. Click it to show the chart. B/S Buy or Sell. An H marks a hedged position. Amount (Lots) The size. The heading follows your size setting (Lots, Amount or Amount, K). Open The price you opened at. Close The price the position would close at now. (To close it, use the \u2715.) Stop / Tr.Stop / Limit Your stop loss, trailing stop distance (pips) and take profit. P/L Gross profit or loss. Com Commission (shown as a negative number). Net P/L Profit or loss after commission and interest, in your account currency. Open Time When the position opened. Ticket Your broker's reference for the position."},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#work-with-several-positions","title":"Work with several positions","text":"<p>Select several rows, then use Bulk Operations or the right-click menu:</p> <ul> <li>Ctrl+Click adds or removes one row, Shift+Click selects a range, Ctrl+A selects all.</li> <li>Escape goes back to a single row.</li> </ul> <p>The right-click menu's Bulk Operations \u25b6 also offers closing all Buy or all Sell positions, or all positions in one instrument. Every bulk action asks you to confirm and says how many positions it will close.</p> Watch how: Select several trades at once (0:44) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#the-right-click-menu","title":"The right-click menu","text":"<p>Right-click a position. Shortcuts are shown beside the items.</p> Watch how: Open-position right-click menu (0:40) <p></p> Item What it does Stop (Set SL) Set or change the stop loss (Alt+T). Limit (Set TP) Set or change the take profit (Alt+L). Trailing Stop Set a trailing stop. Bulk Operations \u25b6 Close many positions at once. Close Position Close it (Alt+C). With several selected it reads, for example, \"Close 3 Positions\". Hedge Position Open the opposite trade (Alt+H). Close with Hedge Only when you hold an opposite position in the same instrument: closes the two against each other. View on Chart Show the instrument on the chart. Copy Trade ID Copy the reference. Export to Excel\u2026 Save the table as a CSV file. Filters / Clear All Filters Show the filter row / remove all filters. <p>If the position has a comment, it is shown near the bottom of the menu.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/open-positions.html#keyboard","title":"Keyboard","text":"<p>Click in the table first.</p> Keys What they do Up / Down, Home / End Move through the rows. Shift+Up / Shift+Down Extend the selection. Ctrl+A Select all rows. Escape goes back to one row. Alt+C (also Delete, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+C) Close the highlighted position (Close Position window). Alt+T / Alt+L Stop loss / take profit. Alt+H Hedge. Alt+E Export to CSV. Menu key Open the right-click menu. <p>Delete and Ctrl+C close a position</p> <p>In this table, Delete and Ctrl+C work like Close Position. With Quick Trade on, they close the position at once, without the Close Position window.</p> <p>The table reads \"No open positions\" when you have none.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html","title":"Pending Orders","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html#pending-orders","title":"Pending Orders","text":"<p>The Pending tab lists your orders that are waiting for their price: entry orders, OCO orders and the like. The number on the tab shows how many you have.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html#what-you-can-do-with-an-order","title":"What you can do with an order","text":"To\u2026 Do this Change its rate or amount Point at the row and click \u270e (or select it and press Enter). See Change or Cancel a Pending Order. Cancel it Click \u2715 on the row, then confirm. Protect it before it fills Right-click it and choose Stop (Pre-defined SL), Limit (Pre-defined TP) or Trailing Stop. See Stop Loss and Take Profit. Cancel many Bulk Operations \u25be: cancel all orders, only limit orders, or only stop orders. You are asked to confirm. Watch how: Change or cancel a pending order (0:52)"},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html#the-columns","title":"The columns","text":"Column What it shows Instrument The instrument. Click it to show the chart. B/S B (Buy) or S (Sell). Amount (Lots) The order size. Order Your broker's order reference. T The order type: ES Entry Stop, EL Entry Limit, S Stop, L Limit. Rate The price that triggers the order. Proximity How far that price is from the market, in pips. Sell / Buy The live Bid and Ask. Tr. Entry / Tr.Stop Trailing entry and trailing stop distances, in pips. Predef. Limit / Predef. Stop The take profit and stop loss that start working when the order fills. Time When the order was placed. <p>Account and Ticket are also shown. Currency, OCO, Trade ID, Created by and Comment can be turned on with Customize\u2026.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html#the-right-click-menu","title":"The right-click menu","text":"<p>Right-click an order to modify or remove it, protect it, add a comment, or cancel many at once.</p> Watch how: Pending-order menu and bulk cancel (0:54) <p></p> Watch how: More with pending orders (0:48) <p></p> Item What it does Modify Order Change the rate or amount (Alt+M). OCO Link Not available in this version. Remove Order Cancel it, after you confirm (Alt+R). With several selected it reads, for example, \"Remove 3 Orders\". Stop (Pre-defined SL) / Limit (Pre-defined TP) / Trailing Stop Protect the position the order will open. Only for a single Entry Stop or Entry Limit order. View on Chart Show the instrument on the chart. Copy Order ID Copy the reference. Comment Add or change a note on the order (up to 50 characters). Bulk Operations \u25b6 Cancel all orders, limit orders or stop orders. Export to Excel\u2026 / Filters / Clear All Filters As on the other tables."},{"location":"trading-tab/pending-orders.html#keyboard","title":"Keyboard","text":"Keys What they do Up / Down, Home / End Move through the rows. Ctrl+Click / Shift+Click, Ctrl+A Select several / all orders. Escape goes back to one. Enter or Alt+M Modify the highlighted order. Alt+R (also Delete, Ctrl+R) Remove the order, after you confirm. Alt+E Export to CSV. Menu key Open the right-click menu. <p>The table reads \"No pending orders\" when you have none.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/status-bar.html","title":"The Account Status Bar","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/status-bar.html#the-account-status-bar","title":"The Account Status Bar","text":"<p>The bar along the bottom of the window always shows the state of your account.</p> <p> </p> <p>Account, Balance, Equity, Usable Margin, Used Margin and Net P/L.</p> Watch how: Find your way around the screen (1:24) <p></p> Field What it means Account(s) The account the figures refer to, with its currency (for example 12345 - USD). With several accounts you can pick one here; All Accounts shows them together. Balance Your cash, not counting open positions. Equity Balance plus the profit or loss of your open positions. UsableMargin What you still have available to trade with. Used Margin What your open positions are holding as collateral. Margin bar Used Margin as a percentage of Equity: green below 100%, amber from 100% to 149%, red from 150%. Net PL The profit or loss of your open positions. A \u26a0 means it is incomplete because a conversion rate is missing. <p>At the right are the Rollover Time and the clock. The \u203a at the far right hides or shows them.</p> <p>Net PL covers open positions only</p> <p>Trades you have closed are not included. For your realised results, see Closed Positions or Analytics.</p> <p>Bonus</p> <p>The text \"(Bonus : 0.00)\" after the Balance is fixed and does not show any bonus on your account.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html","title":"The Watchlist","text":""},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#the-watchlist","title":"The Watchlist","text":"<p>The watchlist on the left of the Trading tab shows live prices. From here you can find any instrument, show it on the chart, and trade it.</p> Watch how: Read the watchlist (1:50) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#find-an-instrument","title":"Find an instrument","text":"<ul> <li>Category tabs: click All, Forex, Crypto, Indices, Commodities, Stocks or ETF. A category only appears if your broker offers instruments of that kind.</li> <li>Search: type in the search box. It matches the symbol and the instrument name, and always searches every instrument, even on your own watchlist tabs. Press Escape or click \u2715 to clear it.</li> <li>Click a row to show the instrument on the chart. Point at a row to see its full name.</li> </ul> <p>The number beside the search box shows how many instruments are listed.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#read-the-prices","title":"Read the prices","text":"Column What it shows SYMBOL The instrument. Always shown. BID The price you sell at, with \u25b2 or \u25bc for the last move. ASK The price you buy at. SPRD The spread: the difference between Bid and Ask. Green when it narrows, red when it widens. HIGH / LOW / % CHG Today's highest Bid, lowest Ask, and the change in %. Hidden until you turn them on (right-click a heading \u2192 Customize columns\u2026). <p>A dash (\u2014) means no price has arrived yet. Click SYMBOL, BID, ASK or SPRD to sort. See Columns and Sorting.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#trade-from-the-watchlist","title":"Trade from the watchlist","text":"To\u2026 Do this Buy Click the Ask price. The Deal Ticket opens on Buy. Sell Click the Bid price. The Deal Ticket opens on Sell. Set a price alert Point at the row and click the \u25b3 that replaces the spread. Open a chart Click the row (or press Alt+N). Watch how: Quick order and hedge (0:41) <p>With Quick Trade on, clicking a price trades at once without the ticket. See One-Click Trading.</p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#make-your-own-watchlist","title":"Make your own watchlist","text":"<ol> <li>Click the + at the right end of the category row.</li> <li>Type a name and click Create. A second row of tabs appears with your watchlist, marked with a star. It starts empty.</li> <li>Go to All, find an instrument, right-click it and choose Add to Watchlist \u25b6 and your watchlist.</li> </ol> Watch how: Make your own watchlist (0:54) <p>Right-click one of your watchlist tabs to Rename\u2026, \u25c0 Move Left, \u25b6 Move Right or Delete Watchlist (you are asked to confirm). To take an instrument out, right-click it on your watchlist's tab and choose Remove from Watchlist.</p> Watch how: Rename, move or delete watchlist tabs (0:46) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#the-right-click-menu","title":"The right-click menu","text":"<p>Right-click an instrument for every action:</p> <p> </p> <p>Chart and alert, market orders, entry orders, OCO orders, and adding to or removing from a watchlist.</p> Watch how: Watchlist right-click menu (1:00) <p></p> Menu item What it does Open Chart Show it on the chart (Alt+N). Price Alert Set an alert (Alt+P). Market Order Buy / Sell Open the Deal Ticket for a market order (Alt+B / Alt+S). Entry Stop / Limit Buy / Sell Open the Deal Ticket for an entry order. See Entry Orders. Entry OCO Buy / Sell Open the Deal Ticket for an OCO order. See OCO Orders. Add to Watchlist \u25b6 Add it to one of your watchlists. Remove from Watchlist Only on your own watchlist tabs. <p>Every order item opens the Deal Ticket first, so you can check the order before sending it. Right-clicking a Bid or Ask price gives a shorter menu with only the Sell or Buy orders, headed by the instrument, side and price.</p> <p> </p> <p>Right-click a price for a short, side-specific menu.</p> Watch how: More from the watchlist (0:46) <p></p>"},{"location":"trading-tab/watchlist.html#keyboard","title":"Keyboard","text":"<p>Click in the list first.</p> Keys What they do Up / Down Move through the list (wraps round). The chart does not change until you press Enter or click. Home / End First / last instrument. Enter Show the instrument on the chart. Alt+B / Alt+S Buy / Sell the highlighted instrument (Deal Ticket, or at once with Quick Trade on). Alt+N / Alt+P Chart / price alert. Alt+F Jump to the search box. Alt+Q Quick Trade on or off. Menu key Open the right-click menu. Escape (in the search box) Clear the search. Left / Right (on the tabs) Move to the next category or watchlist tab."},{"location":"troubleshooting/index.html","title":"Troubleshooting","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/index.html#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","text":"<p>Every problem below is based on a message or behaviour the application actually produces.</p> Problem area Logging In Wrong password, server errors, the server is not in the list Prices and Connection Prices not moving, connection status Placing and Managing Orders Rejected orders, distances, orders placed while offline Display and Layout Missing columns, text size, lost panels Exports and Reports Where exported files go, Reports not available Analytics and Strategies Analytics not loading, strategy status Sound and Voice No sound, no microphone button"},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html","title":"Analytics and Strategies","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html#analytics-and-strategies","title":"Analytics and Strategies","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html#analytics-will-not-load","title":"Analytics will not load","text":"<p>If you see \"Could not load analytics\" with a Retry button, either the connection failed \u2014 press Retry \u2014 or your account is not registered for the analytics service. Managed and master accounts often are not. Contact your broker.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html#strategy-shows-stopped-did-it-fail","title":"strategy shows Stopped \u2014 did it fail?","text":"<p>No. Stopped means it ended normally and is shown with a plain grey badge. A strategy that faulted shows Error with a red badge. Check the Log tab for details. See Strategy status values.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html#i-stopped-a-strategy-but-its-trades-are-still-open","title":"I stopped a strategy but its trades are still open","text":"<p>That is the default \u2014 the stop dialog's two tick boxes start unticked. Tick them to clear the strategy's positions and orders when it stops. See Stopping a strategy.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/analytics-strategies.html#the-tester-will-not-run-my-python-strategy","title":"The Tester will not run my Python strategy","text":"<p>Back-testing supports ActFX scripts only. The message reads \"Back-testing is not available for Python strategies.\" Use Run to execute a Python strategy live.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html","title":"Display and Layout","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#display-and-layout","title":"Display and Layout","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#column-i-need-is-missing","title":"column I need is missing","text":"<p>Right-click the header, choose Customize, and tick it. Several columns are hidden by default.</p> Watch how: Choose and resize table columns (0:40) <p></p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#my-table-looks-different-after-an-update","title":"My table looks different after an update","text":"<p>If an update removes or renames a column, only that column's saved setting is dropped \u2014 the rest of your layout is kept. New columns appear with their default settings. Right-click the header and use Customize to adjust them.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#the-application-reopened-on-a-different-tab","title":"The application reopened on a different tab","text":"<p>The application remembers the last tab you used \u2014 any of the eight \u2014 and reopens on it. See Layout and Profiles.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#the-interface-is-in-english-after-i-chose-another-language","title":"The interface is in English after I chose another language","text":"<p>Only part of the interface is translated in this release. See Settings Before You Log In.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#text-is-too-small-or-too-large","title":"Text is too small or too large","text":"<p>Use the Theme icon on the right-hand strip. The Font Size slider has S, M, L and XL presets and applies everywhere.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/display.html#i-closed-a-floating-window-and-lost-the-panel","title":"I closed a floating window and lost the panel","text":"<p>You did not lose it. The red \u00d7 on a floating window docks the panel back into the main window rather than closing it.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/exports.html","title":"Exports and Reports","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/exports.html#exports-and-reports","title":"Exports and Reports","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/exports.html#where-did-my-exported-csv-go","title":"Where did my exported CSV go?","text":"<p>Into your computer's temporary folder, and it opens automatically. The \"Exported \u2026 rows to CSV\" message shows the full path. Save it from your spreadsheet application if you need to keep it. See Export to CSV.</p> Watch how: Export a table to a spreadsheet (0:39) <p></p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/exports.html#alte-did-nothing","title":"Alt+E did nothing","text":"<p>Click a table first so it has focus. On the Summary tab you will see \"Alt+E \u2014 focus a list first\" if nothing is selected. When a table is focused, Alt+E first opens an Export to CSV window showing what will be saved \u2014 press Export to create the file.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/exports.html#the-reports-tab-says-reports-are-not-available","title":"The Reports tab says reports are not available","text":"<p>The message reads \"Reports not available for this account\". Your broker has not configured report access for this account. Contact your broker.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html","title":"Logging In","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html#logging-in","title":"Logging In","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html#i-get-wrong-account-type-or-username-or-password","title":"I get \"Wrong Account Type or Username or Password\"","text":"<p>Check all three fields. The server must be the one your broker specified \u2014 a live account will not log in to a demo server or the reverse. Passwords are case-sensitive. If Remember me stored an old password, retype it.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html#the-message-mentions-a-server-error-and-says-it-is-not-my-credentials","title":"The message mentions a server error and says it is not my credentials","text":"<p>This is a fault on your broker's server, not something you can fix. Contact your broker's support and quote the message.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html#my-brokers-server-is-not-in-the-server-list","title":"My broker's server is not in the Server list","text":"<p>Click the gear icon on the login card, go to Entries, and add it with the Name, URL and DB Alias your broker gave you. Press Add, then Save.</p> Watch how: Settings on the login screen (0:32) <p></p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/logging-in.html#nothing-happens-when-i-press-login-or-it-times-out","title":"Nothing happens when I press Login, or it times out","text":"<p>If your network uses a proxy, set it under the gear icon \u2192 Connection. Otherwise check your internet connection and any firewall.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html","title":"Placing and Managing Orders","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#placing-and-managing-orders","title":"Placing and Managing Orders","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#my-order-was-rejected-what-does-the-message-mean","title":"My order was rejected \u2014 what does the message mean?","text":"<p>The reason is shown under \"Order failed\". It may come from your broker or from the application's own checks. Common causes: the size is outside the instrument's minimum or maximum (\"The amount must be not less than \u2026 and not more than \u2026 lots\"); the price is too close to the market (see the next item); insufficient usable margin; or the market is closed.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#it-says-the-rate-must-be-a-certain-distance-from-the-market","title":"It says the rate must be a certain distance from the market","text":"<p>Your broker sets a minimum distance for pending orders and for stops and limits. The Deal Ticket shows the nearest valid price and a \"Use this\" button that fills it in for you.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#i-cannot-set-a-stop-or-limit-from-the-chart","title":"I cannot set a stop or limit from the chart","text":"<p>Setting a stop or limit on the chart works the same way as the Stop and Limit dialogs. If your broker refuses it, \"Order failed\" shows the reason. You can always use the Stop and Limit columns in Open Positions instead \u2014 click the cell to open the dialog.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#i-closed-a-position-by-accident","title":"I closed a position by accident","text":"<p>A close cannot be reversed. Normally closing a single position opens the Close Position window, so nothing closes until you confirm. With Quick Trade on, closing acts at once \u2014 turn Quick Trade off with Alt+Q if you would rather confirm each close. See Open Positions.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#i-placed-orders-during-an-outage-where-are-they","title":"I placed orders during an outage \u2014 where are they?","text":"<p>They were held and submitted as pending orders when the connection returned. Look on the Pending tab. See 11.3.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/orders.html#removing-a-stop-or-take-profit-did-not-ask-me-to-confirm","title":"Removing a stop or take-profit did not ask me to confirm","text":"<p>Correct \u2014 the Remove button in the Stop Loss and Take Profit dialogs acts immediately. Set it again if that was not intended.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html","title":"Prices and Connection","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html#prices-and-connection","title":"Prices and Connection","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html#the-indicator-says-no-prices-retrying","title":"The indicator says \"No Prices \u2014 retrying\u2026\"","text":"<p>The price feed has stalled. Your session is still open and the last known prices are shown, but they are not moving. The application reconnects by itself \u2014 wait for the indicator to turn green before trading. See Connection Status.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html#the-indicator-says-offline-reconnecting","title":"The indicator says \"Offline \u2014 reconnecting\u2026\"","text":"<p>Your session with the broker was lost and the application is logging you back in. You may also see the message \"Offline mode \u2014 simulated prices\". Do not trade until the indicator turns green. Orders placed meanwhile are held and later sent as pending orders \u2014 see 11.3.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html#prices-are-frozen-but-the-indicator-is-green","title":"Prices are frozen but the indicator is green","text":"<p>Check whether the market for that instrument is open. Some instruments also have a daily no-trade break, shown in the NT Interval column on the Instruments tab.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/prices.html#the-watchlist-all-tab-shows-no-moving-prices","title":"The watchlist \"All\" tab shows no moving prices","text":"<p>On a broker with a very large instrument list, the All tab does not subscribe to every instrument \u2014 that would be tens of thousands of price streams. Create a watchlist with the instruments you care about and prices will update there.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/sound-voice.html","title":"Sound and Voice","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/sound-voice.html#sound-and-voice","title":"Sound and Voice","text":""},{"location":"troubleshooting/sound-voice.html#i-hear-no-sounds-even-with-sounds-enabled","title":"I hear no sounds even with sounds enabled","text":"<p>Check three switches: Show notifications in Settings \u2192 Trading (when it is off, sounds are silenced too), the main sounds switch, and the tick box for that particular event. Also check the volume slider and your computer's volume. See 10.10.</p>"},{"location":"troubleshooting/sound-voice.html#the-microphone-button-is-missing","title":"The microphone button is missing","text":"<p>It appears only when speech is configured for your installation and you are connected. If it is present but blocked, the panel explains whether the build lacks audio support, the speech key is missing, or no microphone was found.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/index.html","title":"Configuring Your Workspace","text":""},{"location":"workspace/index.html#configuring-your-workspace","title":"Configuring Your Workspace","text":"<p>ActTrader lets you arrange the screen the way you like to work. Your layout is saved automatically, separately for each account.</p> <p> </p> <p>From top to bottom: the top bar, the tab row, the work area for the tab you are on, and the account bar.</p> Watch how: Find your way around the screen (1:24) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/index.html#the-parts-of-the-window","title":"The parts of the window","text":"Area What it contains Top bar Your broker's logo with a \u25be (click it to switch accounts), the connection status, your account number and profile name, and a button to show or hide the right-hand icon strip. Tab row The eight tabs. On the Trading tab this row also holds the chart controls (New chart, Linked, the layout picker and the \u25a6 button that turns charts off and on). On a narrow window these fold away behind a single \u203a. The ? at the right starts a guided tour of the tab you are on. Work area Changes with the tab you are on. Account bar Your Balance, Equity, Usable Margin, Used Margin and Net P/L, the margin bar, and at the right the rollover time and clock. See The Account Status Bar."},{"location":"workspace/index.html#make-it-your-own","title":"Make it your own","text":"To\u2026 Read Use the theme, panels, news and help icons The Right-Hand Icon Strip Keep more than one account in the app Using More Than One Account Save different layouts and switch between them Layout and Profiles Move a panel or chart to a second monitor Floating Windows Choose, reorder and resize table columns Columns Sort and filter any table Sorting \u00b7 Filtering Save a table to a spreadsheet Export to CSV"},{"location":"workspace/accounts.html","title":"Using More Than One Account","text":""},{"location":"workspace/accounts.html#using-more-than-one-account","title":"Using More Than One Account","text":"<p>You can keep several accounts in ActTrader and switch between them without typing your details again.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/accounts.html#add-an-account","title":"Add an account","text":"<ol> <li>Click your broker's logo (with the \u25be) at the top left.</li> <li>Click Add new account\u2026 at the top of the list.</li> <li>Enter the Server, Login and Password, as on the login screen, and click Login.</li> </ol> <p>The account is checked with your broker, then added to the list.</p> <p> </p> <p>The Add Account window, with the same fields as the login screen.</p> Watch how: Add and switch accounts (0:35) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/accounts.html#switch-account","title":"Switch account","text":"<ol> <li>Click the logo at the top left. The list shows all your saved accounts, with a tick beside the one you are using.</li> <li>Click another account.</li> </ol> <p>Add new account\u2026 at the top, then your saved accounts; the tick marks the one you are using.</p> <p>The app logs out and logs in to the other account. A Switching account\u2026 message shows which account you are moving from and to.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/accounts.html#remove-an-account","title":"Remove an account","text":"<p>Click the \u2715 beside an account in the list, then confirm. Its saved login details are deleted from this computer. You cannot remove the account you are using, or your last remaining account.</p> <p>Each account keeps its own setup</p> <p>Watchlists, column layouts, panel sizes, floating windows, chart setups and strategies are saved separately for each account. Switching accounts switches all of them; nothing you change for one account affects another.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/columns.html","title":"Columns","text":""},{"location":"workspace/columns.html#columns","title":"Columns","text":"<p>You can choose which columns a table shows, put them in the order you like, and change their width. Your changes are saved.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/columns.html#show-or-hide-columns","title":"Show or hide columns","text":"<ol> <li>Right-click any column header and choose Customize\u2026.</li> <li>Tick the columns you want and untick the ones you don't. (Double-clicking a row or pressing Space does the same.)</li> <li>To change the order, select a column and use \u25b2 and \u25bc (or Ctrl+Up / Ctrl+Down).</li> <li>Click Ok.</li> </ol> <p>Default puts back the original columns, order and widths.</p> <p> </p> <p>Every column of the table, each with a tick box, and the buttons to change the order.</p> Watch how: Choose and resize table columns (0:40) <p></p> <p>Some columns cannot be hidden, such as Symbol or Instrument; their tick box is dimmed. At least one column must stay visible.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/columns.html#change-a-columns-width","title":"Change a column's width","text":"<ul> <li>Drag the divider at the right edge of the column's header. Only that column changes.</li> <li>Double-click the divider to fit the column to its contents.</li> <li>Or right-click the header and choose Set width to fit data.</li> </ul> <p>Right-click any column header for these two options.</p> <p>Bid and Ask columns never shrink below the width their prices need.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/columns.html#where-you-can-reorder-columns","title":"Where you can reorder columns","text":"<p>You can show, hide and resize columns on every table. You can also reorder them on the Open, Pending and Closed tables, the Instruments tab, and the Accounts and Positions tables of the Summary tab. On the watchlist and the other Summary tables the order is fixed.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/export.html","title":"Export to CSV","text":""},{"location":"workspace/export.html#export-to-csv","title":"Export to CSV","text":"<p>You can save any table as a CSV file and open it in a spreadsheet such as Excel.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/export.html#export-a-table","title":"Export a table","text":"<ol> <li>Click Export CSV on the table's toolbar. You can also right-click the table and choose Export to Excel\u2026, or press Alt+E on the Open, Pending and Closed tables and on the Summary tab.</li> <li>A window shows the table's name and how many rows and columns will be saved. Click Export (or press Enter).</li> </ol> <p>The file opens in your spreadsheet program, and a message tells you how many rows were saved and where.</p> <p> </p> <p>The table name, the number of rows and columns, and the Export and Cancel buttons.</p> Watch how: Export a table to a spreadsheet (0:39) <p></p> <p>The file contains exactly what you see in the table, with your current sorting, filters and search. If the table is empty, you are warned that the file will contain only the column headings.</p> <p>Save the file if you need to keep it</p> <p>Exported files are written to a temporary folder and opened straight away. Temporary files can be deleted when your computer restarts, so use Save As in your spreadsheet program to keep a copy.</p> <p>\"Export to Excel\u2026\" saves a CSV file, which Excel opens normally.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/filtering.html","title":"Filtering","text":""},{"location":"workspace/filtering.html#filtering","title":"Filtering","text":"<p>Filters show only the rows you want, for example only EURUSD trades or only trades opened today.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/filtering.html#filter-a-table","title":"Filter a table","text":"<ol> <li>Click Filters on the table's toolbar (or right-click the table and choose Filters). A filter row appears under the column headers.</li> <li>Click the filter cell under the column you want to filter.</li> <li>Set the filter in the window that opens, then click OK.</li> </ol> <p>The table now shows only matching rows. Filters on several columns work together: a row must match all of them.</p> <p> </p> <p>With Filters on, a filter cell appears under each column header.</p> Watch how: Sort and filter a table (0:53) <p></p> Watch how: Filter a table (0:48) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/filtering.html#the-four-kinds-of-filter","title":"The four kinds of filter","text":"<p>The window that opens depends on the kind of column.</p> Column Filter How it works Text, such as Comment Contain Type some text; rows that contain it are kept. Numbers, such as Amount or P/L Range Choose &gt;=, &lt;=, = or Between and enter the value(s). A set of values, such as Instrument or B/S Visible / Invisible Move values between the two lists with the arrow buttons or by double-clicking. Only values in Visible are kept. Date and time Current Day / Current Shift / From \u2026 Till Tick one or more; a row is kept if it matches any of them. Enter dates as YYYY-MM-DD and times as HH:MM. <p> </p> <p>Values in Visible are kept; move the others to Invisible.</p> <p> </p> <p>Choose an operator and enter the value.</p> <p> </p> <p>Rows containing the text you type are kept.</p> <p> </p> <p>Tick any combination of periods.</p> <p>Each window has Apply (apply and keep the window open), OK and Cancel.</p> <p>Current Day and Current Shift in table filters</p> <p>In these filters, Current Day means today on your computer's clock, and Current Shift means the last eight hours.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/filtering.html#clear-filters","title":"Clear filters","text":"<p>While a filter is on, a \u2715 shows on the Filters button and a \u2715 Clear button appears at the end of the filter row. Either one removes all filters on that table. Clear All Filters is also in the right-click menu.</p> <p>An empty filter is removed</p> <p>If you leave a filter's box empty, or move every value to Invisible, that filter is simply removed and all rows come back. No message is shown.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html","title":"Floating Windows","text":""},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html#floating-windows","title":"Floating Windows","text":"<p>You can move most panels, and extra charts, into windows of their own. This is useful with a second monitor.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html#move-a-panel-into-its-own-window","title":"Move a panel into its own window","text":"<ol> <li>Right-click the panel's tab (or its toolbar) and choose \u21f2 Undock to floating window.</li> <li>Drag the new window by its title bar to wherever you want it, including another screen.</li> </ol> <p>Right-click a tab to move it into its own window.</p> Watch how: Pop out charts and panels (0:40) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html#put-it-back","title":"Put it back","text":"<p>Click the X at the right of the floating window's title bar, or right-click its title bar and choose Dock back to main window. The panel returns to the main window; nothing is lost.</p> Button What it does \u2212 Minimise the window. \u2610 Maximise it, or restore it. X Dock the panel back into the main window. <p>The buttons follow the style of your computer: on Windows and Linux they sit at the right of the title bar; on a Mac they are the red, yellow and green buttons at the left.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html#open-extra-chart-windows","title":"Open extra chart windows","text":"<p>Click New chart above the charts on the Trading tab. Each chart window can show a different instrument, and you can open up to six. The X closes a chart window.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/floating-windows.html#combine-panels-in-one-window","title":"Combine panels in one window","text":"<p>When another panel is floating in a window of its own, a + appears in the title bar. Click it and pick that panel. They become tabs in the same window. To separate a tab again, drag it out of the tab strip, or use its \u21f2 button. Each tab's \u00d7 docks just that panel back.</p> Watch how: Combine floating windows (0:45) <p></p> <p>Floating windows and their positions are remembered next time you start the app.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/icon-strip.html","title":"The Right-Hand Icon Strip","text":""},{"location":"workspace/icon-strip.html#the-right-hand-icon-strip","title":"The Right-Hand Icon Strip","text":"<p>The narrow strip on the right edge of the window gives you quick access to the theme, panels, news, help and settings. Click an icon to open its panel; press Escape or click elsewhere to close it.</p> <p> </p> <p>The icons down the right edge of the window, with the Help panel open.</p> Watch how: Use the settings icons (1:27) <p></p> Icon Opens What you can do \u25c9 Profiles Switch between your saved layouts or create a new one. See Layout and Profiles. \u25d1 Theme Choose Dark or Light, and the font size (S, M, L, XL or the slider). \u25a6 Panels Show or hide the News panel, the account bar and the chart's bottom bar. The chart's Bid and Ask lines are in Chart Settings \u2192 Scales (see Layout and Appearance). \u2261 News Feeds Add or remove news sources, or reset them to the defaults. \u2699 Settings The full Settings window. See Settings. ? Help The Trader Manual (F1), the keyboard shortcut list (Shift+F1), and the update check. The bottom line shows the app version."},{"location":"workspace/icon-strip.html#change-the-theme-or-font-size","title":"Change the theme or font size","text":"<ol> <li>Click \u25d1.</li> <li>Click Light or Dark. The whole app, charts included, switches straight away.</li> <li>Use the font size buttons or the slider to make all text smaller or bigger.</li> </ol> <p>Your choice is saved with your profile.</p> Watch how: Change the theme and font size (0:34) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/icon-strip.html#check-for-updates","title":"Check for updates","text":"<p>Open ? (Help). When a new version is available it says Update available with a Download button; otherwise click Check for updates.</p> Watch how: Command palette, Help and sounds (1:07) <p></p> <p>Hide the strip</p> <p>Use the button at the right of the top bar to hide the strip and give the work area more room. Click it again to bring the strip back.</p> <p>When voice commands are set up, a microphone button also appears on the strip. See Voice Commands.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/layout-and-profiles.html","title":"Layout and Profiles","text":""},{"location":"workspace/layout-and-profiles.html#layout-and-profiles","title":"Layout and Profiles","text":""},{"location":"workspace/layout-and-profiles.html#your-layout-is-saved-automatically","title":"Your layout is saved automatically","text":"<p>You don't need to save anything. When you start ActTrader again you get back:</p> <ul> <li>the tab you were on and the size of every panel,</li> <li>your column widths, order and choices for every table,</li> <li>your watchlists and their order,</li> <li>floating windows and where they were,</li> <li>chart setups and templates,</li> <li>your theme, font size and all your settings.</li> </ul> <p>All of this is kept separately for each account.</p>"},{"location":"workspace/layout-and-profiles.html#keep-several-layouts-with-profiles","title":"Keep several layouts with profiles","text":"<p>A profile is a named layout. For example, one for scalping with several charts, and one for watching the market with a large watchlist. Anything you change is saved to the profile you are using.</p> <p>Create a profile</p> <ol> <li>Click \u25c9 (Profiles) on the right-hand strip.</li> <li>Type a name and click Create. The new profile starts with the standard layout.</li> <li>Arrange the screen the way you want it.</li> </ol> <p>Switch profile: open \u25c9 and click another profile.</p> <p>Delete a profile: open \u25c9 and click the \u2715 beside it. It is deleted straight away, without a question, so check the name first.</p> <p> </p> <p>The profile you are using at the top, your other profiles below, and the box for creating a new one.</p> Watch how: Save screen layouts as profiles (0:37) <p></p> Watch how: Delete a profile (0:22) <p></p>"},{"location":"workspace/sorting.html","title":"Sorting","text":""},{"location":"workspace/sorting.html#sorting","title":"Sorting","text":"<p>Click a column header to sort the table by that column.</p> <ul> <li>First click: sort one way. An arrow (\u25b2 or \u25bc) appears in the header.</li> <li>Second click: sort the other way.</li> <li>Third click: back to the table's normal order.</li> </ul> <p> </p> <p>The column used for sorting is highlighted and marked with an arrow.</p> Watch how: Sort and filter a table (0:53) <p></p> <p>The sort you choose on the watchlist and the Instruments tab is remembered next time you start the app. Other tables go back to their normal order.</p>"}]}